ns":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T04:57:02-07:00","id":285821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=285487#post285487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a matter of fact, she is not. Her original description was someone who took the shapes of good-looking youths, which overs a wide ground of ages but tends toward much more mature-looking appearances than that of a loli.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have my Eight-Hundred Penis Battle-form Bishop, if you MUST, but I'm with Jen on this. You can have my Lolicon Raksi when you pry her from my-- yeah, I'm not gonna finish that sentence,-- *hrmmms*<br /> <br /> Suchi is on his own, though. Seriously, Jen, even in satire-- you defend Suchi?? I am disappoint.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T05:41:02-07:00","id":285826,"title":"","content":"As a villain I would defend him. Suchi is the Big Bad Wolf. No really, he is. The original version of the story of Red Riding hood Red's observations were, eyes, ears, and leg. The original story was a warning to little girls about the dangers in the world not of being killed, but raped. Also the original version, there was no woodsman.<br /> <br /> Chances are the Lunar elder will stay very, very disturbing. Jen look at 1e references to these characters and you will see the changes might be that Raksi is more prone to killing and eating you rather than letting you use her library. Her library, might even just be a trap to lure in helpless victims searching for knowledge so she can have a steady stream of human prey walk into her web.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T06:24:55-07:00","id":285838,"title":"","content":"I like the fact that the elder Lunars are so screwy, because Lunars are kind of good guys: I mean, they're not the Abyssals, or Infernals. They want to protect Creation. But the elders are nuts... because that's how the great curse works.<br /> I don't necessarily love every single one, and think they're written brilliantly (Lilith seems kind of dull to me, for example), but I'm happy with the idea of the oldest Lunars for the most part being nutcases who are too powerful for anyone to force to behave.<br /> I like Ma-Ha-Suchi because he's a bad guy who's powerful enough to be a threat to an entire direction, but not to the silly extent of a Deathlord. Ie he's a threat that it's reasonable to expect a circle of PCs to take down as an end boss at low to mid xp.<br /> So I hope they don't completely rewrite them... but I don't think they will. I think they'll fiddle around with them a bit.<br /> Though I wouldn't be surprised if Tammuz gets rewritten the most, if only because the TSR's being taken out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T08:06:53-07:00","id":285925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=285479#post285479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does NSFT mean, anyway? Not Safe for Twitter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I thought everybody know that NSFT mean Not Safe for Wor.............uhwhoot.........Eh, Safe for Transformer as Lioness point out. Cause you know, Icky Elder Lunar sex is Icky and all..... <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/832db6e1-79a6-4ba3-8ab2-58bc9680697a.jpg~original\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 10-18-2014, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T08:10:47-07:00","id":285927,"title":"","content":"The game has wasted enough time and words on the First Age Elders by now. I'd rather hear about new characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T21:33:04-07:00","id":286373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=285821#post285821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can have my Eight-Hundred Penis Battle-form Bishop, if you MUST, but I'm with Jen on this. You can have my Lolicon Raksi when you pry her from my-- yeah, I'm not gonna finish that sentence,-- *hrmmms*</div> </div> </div> </div>You ruined a perfectly good opportunity to post the Edgar Suit scene from Men in Black. You monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T22:45:19-07:00","id":286403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=285927#post285927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game has wasted enough time and words on the First Age Elders by now. I'd rather hear about new characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it maybe devoted too much of the wrong kind of attention to them in 2e, but the Lunar Elders are still an important part of the game -- they're something that makes Lunars distinct (Sidereal and DB elders are very different in nature and relation to younger Exalted, and Solars / Abyssals / Infernals don't have them at all, although Abyssals and Infernals have sort-of stand-ins -- more specifically, Sidereal elders are occluded from the world, while aside from the Empress DB elders don't generally get that old and powerful. The DLs are mostly unknown, and the Demon Princes are both unknown and sealed. That means that from the perspective of the mortal world, the Lunar elders are perhaps some of the most powerful and terrifying beings active in Creation, which has implications for Lunars as a whole.)<br /> <br /> They also do serve an important role as potential antagonists. I think 2e overplayed them as that (and made them very one-note and comparatively boring, which tended to lead to them seeing a bit less use for that purpose anyhow, especially when the more vibrant Infernal stuff started to appear), but the idea of Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi as boogieman who parents use to scare young DBs to sleep is still a key bit of Lunar presence in the setting. I think that one thing the Lunar books could talk about a bit more is how these people's reputations shape the <i>image</i> of Lunars and therefore the way you will be seen as a Lunar yourself in much of the world.<br /> <br /> (For people who read Tower of God, I'm thinking about how the legends of the other Irregulars shape how people look at Baam -- only one of them has actually appeared, and only for like a few pages, but they've had a huge impact in terms of defining what it means to be an Irregular and therefore the nature of the story.)<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously being associated with Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi has its drawbacks (even if 3e makes them less insane, their reputations will probably be about what they've always been), but they also represent (and, by extension, make all Lunars represent) this exaggerated symbol of fear and power which younger Lunars can exploit. In that respect talking about Ma-Ha-Suchi a bit <i>is</i> talking about your character, or at least their public image. Some people might object to having Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi as the public face of Lunars, but, I mean -- you're Anathema; that's what it means. And naturally the fact that they've become the public face of Lunars is not an accident; first, their reputations are probably exaggerated by Immaculates, and second, I suspect the Immaculates very deliberately play up the most scary, insane-seeming Lunars out there.<br /> <br /> The important part is to write them (at least in the Lunars manual) more in terms of what they mean for your character, what sort of stories they're useful for (both when using them directly and when you're invoking that reputation indirectly), that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-19-2014, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T23:07:25-07:00","id":286433,"title":"","content":"That's a very important point, I think, that these are the faces of the Lunars. They show you why people hate and fear Anathema: when you say Anathema, the first thing that pops into people's head is the infamous Ma-Ha-Suchi, or people like him, savages who want to destroy civilization with their armies of man-eating beastmen.<br /> Someone's got to be that, so that you can say why people swallow the Immaculate's lies: because they're not completely lies. When they say &quot;Anathema are goat-shagging nutjobs who want to feed you to beastmen&quot; people believe it, because to some extent it's true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T23:55:39-07:00","id":286452,"title":"","content":"I recall a statement that they could probably manage a bit more nuance on the Lunar Elders (said of Ma-Ha, inferred for the rest of 'em). It's unlikely to impact that public perception much, mind you, but should be enough to make interacting with them for any splat -- <i>especially</i> Lunars -- into a less one-note experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T05:53:37-07:00","id":286569,"title":"","content":"I hope Raksi continues to be a reference to a 1970s TV show and a reminder that Exalted: the Lunars was written by people who weren't anywhere near as smart as they thought they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T06:23:59-07:00","id":286579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286403#post286403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it maybe devoted too much of the wrong kind of attention to them in 2e, but the Lunar Elders are still an important part of the game -- they're something that makes Lunars distinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Lunars should have <i>Elders</i>. Just not these ones, because I'm sick of them.<br /> <br /> Ideally, I'd want fewer &quot;important&quot; people and First Age survivors, and more local Elders. Ma-ha-suchi is pretty much a fixture of the setting, but he shouldn't really <i>matter</i> to Lunars\u2013 to anyone \u2013 in, say, Jiara. If Jiara has Lunar bogeys, they should really be closer to home, and this goes for vast majority of Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T06:31:11-07:00","id":286580,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm all for new Lunar Elder since the old one left a bad taste in my mouth. And seriously, who here will boycott the game if it don't have Raski or Ma-Ha-Suchi anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T08:24:03-07:00","id":286630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286579#post286579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Lunars should have <i>Elders</i>. Just not these ones, because I'm sick of them.<br /> <br /> Ideally, I'd want fewer &quot;important&quot; people and First Age survivors, and more local Elders. Ma-ha-suchi is pretty much a fixture of the setting, but he shouldn't really <i>matter</i> to Lunars\u2013 to anyone \u2013 in, say, Jiara. If Jiara has Lunar bogeys, they should really be closer to home, and this goes for vast majority of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, but there is around 300 or so at any given time, so a few detailed ones shouldn't really get anyone up in a tizzy. I've always interpreted them as examples of the madness Elders can go to rather than what the defacto Elder is. Elders most likely know of one another too, since again there is only around 300 of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T10:34:22-07:00","id":286747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286630#post286630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, but there is around 300 or so at any given time, so a few detailed ones shouldn't really get anyone up in a tizzy. I've always interpreted them as examples of the madness Elders can go to rather than what the defacto Elder is. Elders most likely know of one another too, since again there is only around 300 of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trope where most elder Lunars are irredeemably insane or pathetically mopey is just out of hand. The one elder Lunar I can think of who isn't like that is Tamuz, and he hasn't even done much in a long time. <br /> <br /> I wish at least 1 Lunar elder was written up in a manner that portrayed them as half as nuanced, interesting, cunning, or smart as Chejop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T10:47:15-07:00","id":286756,"title":"","content":"Stephen Lea Sheppard on Raksi:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The question is &quot;How can we keep Raksi herself, i.e. in fullfillment of her own archetype, while making her a deep, interesting, and useful enough character to not be a fucking waste of wordcount?&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T10:55:31-07:00","id":286785,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the problem wasn't the First Age Elders, but the lack of Second Age Elders.<br /> <br /> I suppose that on some levels it makes sense; the First Age Elders are powerful and iconic, up there with the Deathlords and the like. The non-monstrous Elders were also those who had things they cared about threw themselves into the fight, first against the Great Contagion, then against the Balorian Crusade. Most of them probably died as a consequence. Meanwhile, the First Age Elders, being more powerful and - YCMV - less involved with the world at large, and thus were comparatively more likely to survive.<br /> <br /> Still, even if we assume the first crop of reincarnations went through crazy mortality rates in the fucked up world immediately post-Crusade, there should be some survivors, and after a century or two things ought to have mostly stabilised. Which means the majority of Elders - arguably a significant portion of all Lunars, again YCMV - should actually be one to five hundred year old, and significant powers in their own right. But we don't really know about these; the only one I can think of off-hand is Gerd Marrow-Eater (200-ish years old), who was retconned into being the creator of Haslanti.<br /> <br /> Where are the legendary monsters? The wandering silver heroes? The strange patron deities? Give us examples of the guys likely to track down a newly exalted Lunar and out-race, out-smart or just plain scare off the Wyld Hunt in the process. Show us where they take them, the hidden cities and forgotten kingdoms and forbidden lands where silver Stewards rule over beast and man and god. Tell us of the legends they share, about the world and the Exalted, the truths and the lies.<br /> <br /> In fact, fuck it; I'm <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/286764-the-silver-host-a-community-resource\">making a thread for it</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:19:50-07:00","id":286803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286747#post286747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trope where most elder Lunars are irredeemably insane or pathetically mopey is just out of hand. The one elder Lunar I can think of who isn't like that is Tamuz, and he hasn't even done much in a long time.<br /> <br /> I wish at least 1 Lunar elder was written up in a manner that portrayed them as half as nuanced, interesting, cunning, or smart as Chejop.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, which is why I said they're of the madness they can go to, not the madness they WILL go to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:26:52-07:00","id":286810,"title":"","content":"Raksi? A waste of wordcount? Her 2e write-up seemed effective for my purposes; motivating my PCs to kill her and take her stuff. Raksi is <i>near-irredeemably</i><i> evil</i>, from an RPG perspective, this is not necessarily a bad thing. Having a few <i>obvious </i>villains in a setting isn't bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:33:40-07:00","id":286814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286810#post286810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi is <i>irredeemably evil</i>, from an RPG perspective, this is not necessarily a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was your takeaway about Raksi then the write-up failed miserably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:51:28-07:00","id":286824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286814#post286814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was your takeaway about Raksi then the write-up failed miserably.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think so. My players got to vanquish some evil, preserve civilization in the Southeast, and the Twilight Caste got a really frikkin' sweet... shawl artifact, thing, out of it.<br /> <br /> Do you even RPG bro? In-character motivation ==&gt; Dungeon ==&gt; Monsters/Traps ==&gt; Boss ==&gt; ??? ==&gt; Loot/Renown. That's a perfect session. If the write up causes this to happen, then it's a good write up. If a character is written up in such a way that in <i>facilitates PC action </i>and several session's worth of game play, then it's a good write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:51:51-07:00","id":286825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286756#post286756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stephen Lea Sheppard on Raksi:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The question is &quot;How can we keep Raksi herself, i.e. in fullfillment of her own archetype, while making her a deep, interesting, and useful enough character to not be a fucking waste of wordcount?&quot; </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I vote &quot;Change the basis of her character from She-Who-Must-Be-Obeyed to (Colonel) Kurtz.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:56:37-07:00","id":286826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286825#post286825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vote &quot;Change the basis of her character from She-Who-Must-Be-Obeyed to (Colonel) Kurtz.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_%28Tarzan%29\" target=\"_blank\">Queen La</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-19-2014, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T11:59:47-07:00","id":286829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286825#post286825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vote &quot;Change the basis of her character from She-Who-Must-Be-Obeyed to (Colonel) Kurtz.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Stephen, in the post I took that quote from, the basis for Raksi is the original Rakshasa of Indian mythology, a shapeshifting cannibalistic trickster demon - in fact, she predates the Fair Folk being named raksha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T12:15:23-07:00","id":286834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286824#post286824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think so. My players got to vanquish some evil, preserve civilization in the Southeast, and the Twilight Caste got a really frikkin' sweet... shawl artifact, thing, out of it.<br /> <br /> Do you even RPG bro? In-character motivation ==&gt; Dungeon ==&gt; Monsters/Traps ==&gt; Boss ==&gt; ??? ==&gt; Loot/Renown. That's a perfect session. If the write up causes this to happen, then it's a good write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need to set up reasons to dungeon crawl. You just do. If that results in military adventurism with questionable outcomes on the ethical front, well, this is Exalted, and those are the problems faced by characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T12:23:37-07:00","id":286841,"title":"","content":"One of the writing team did a post about Raksi, about how, yes, she is insane, but she's also intelligent and smart, and has chosen to present herself in such a way as to create a particular impression in those whom she talks with... ah, found it:<a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-competence-and-raksi\" target=\"_blank\"> On Competence and Raksi</a>, from Stephen.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:the-silver-plan\" target=\"_blank\">The Silver Plan</a>, also by Stephen, may be relevant in explaining what she's doing with her lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T12:26:29-07:00","id":286845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286834#post286834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't really need to set up reasons to dungeon crawl. You just do. If that results in military adventurism with questionable outcomes on the ethical front, well, this is Exalted, and those are the problems faced by characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... kinda do unless you're a Scavenger Lord. Entering a dungeon without some kind of <i>goal</i> just feels clumsy and gamey; it breaks your immersion.<br /> <br /> And furthermore, questionable ethical outcomes? About killing Raksi? There are none; she's a threat to civilized peoples everywhere (and my PCs were, if nothing else, champions of civilization, so it worked in <i>my </i>campaign) and literally kiddnaps and <i>eats babies.</i> You've done Creation a favor by freeing up her Exaltation for a new, less diabolical host.<br /> <br /> If you want a <i>really evil fucker</i> for your PCs to kill in the Southeast, Raksi is perfect the way she is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T12:32:58-07:00","id":286850,"title":"","content":"Sorry, this is still fun. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Raksi is a shapeshifting cannibal whose Tell is that her hands are backwards. Remind you of anything? </div> </div> </div>Writers who didn't do their homework into where Gary Gygax got his ideas from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T12:46:09-07:00","id":286854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286826#post286826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_%28Tarzan%29\" target=\"_blank\">Queen La</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like King Louie.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://38.media.tumblr.com/db591ea8edc8da16e84fbce0ababc716/tumblr_n2xtcgJPEr1tqs1heo1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T13:04:45-07:00","id":286868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286824#post286824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you even RPG bro? In-character motivation ==&gt; Dungeon ==&gt; Monsters/Traps ==&gt; Boss ==&gt; ??? ==&gt; Loot/Renown. That's a perfect session. If the write up causes this to happen, then it's a good write up. If a character is written up in such a way that in <i>facilitates PC action </i>and several session's worth of game play, then it's a good write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah dude, I have a real problem with NPCs in a game like Exalted (i.e. one where Detect Evil is not a thing at least in part because objective evil is also not a thing, where most of the the Big Bad Things of the setting are usually presented as alien/amoral by reasonable human standards instead of Eeeeevil) being set up as objectively-evil. And I consider write-ups presented without any nuance to be defective on that note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T13:15:14-07:00","id":286878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286868#post286868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah dude, I have a real problem with NPCs in a game like Exalted (i.e. one where Detect Evil is not a thing at least in part because objective evil is also not a thing, where most of the the Big Bad Things of the setting are usually presented as alien/amoral by reasonable human standards instead of Eeeeevil) being set up as objectively-evil. And I consider write-ups presented without any nuance to be defective on that note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah. Nuance can be a hard thing to get into a character. It allows one to do things with a character beyond the outline you've provided. But if objective good/evil is all you want out of the character in your games? Airbrushing out the nuance is trivial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T13:40:14-07:00","id":286893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286868#post286868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah dude, I have a real problem with NPCs in a game like Exalted (i.e. one where Detect Evil is not a thing at least in part because objective evil is also not a thing, where most of the the Big Bad Things of the setting are usually presented as alien/amoral by reasonable human standards instead of Eeeeevil) being set up as objectively-evil. And I consider write-ups presented without any nuance to be defective on that note.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You sound like you're hung up on the word evil rather than the concept because the word evil has a DnD alignment context for you. As setting the world back on a path of righteousness and progress is <i>very</i> in-theme for a Solar campaign, this is a silly, unhelpful hang-up to have. You don't learn Raksi is evil by casting <i>detect evil</i> encompassing a square she occupies; you learn Raksi is evil when she sends her ape men to loot, rape and pillage across the Southeast and you happen to be in her way.<br /> <br /> And more importantly, with the unambiguously evil Raksi narrative I ran with, my players had <i>hella </i><i>fun</i>. You remember <i>fun </i>don't you? Celebrating Exalted specifically because it's different is not conducive to a fun experience; you'll avoid good ideas and entertaining elements just because &quot;well, <i>other</i> RPGs do that! Get it out of my Exalted! It's not original!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T13:54:48-07:00","id":286898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286824#post286824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you even RPG bro? In-character motivation ==&gt; Dungeon ==&gt; Monsters/Traps ==&gt; Boss ==&gt; ??? ==&gt; Loot/Renown. That's a perfect session. If the write up causes this to happen, then it's a good write up. If a character is written up in such a way that in <i>facilitates PC action </i>and several session's worth of game play, then it's a good write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty easy for a Solar or Lunar PCs to hit Raksi with an an opening move that kills her outright. Even as a monster that's there just to be killed she's not a particularly satisfying opponent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T14:00:19-07:00","id":286904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286898#post286898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty easy for a Solar or Lunar PCs to hit Raksi with an an opening move that kills her outright. Even as a monster that's there just to be killed she's not a particularly satisfying opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This problem is solved with <i>very basic </i>encounter design.<br /> <br /> Her boss fight in my campaign consisted of her standing up on a balcony doing her best evil villian laugh and throwing humiliating quips (and spells!) around while the PCs fought her summoned minions. That's how a Raksi encounter should be handled, IMO; you're using her potential in an encounter incorrectly if it's a straight on fight. After all that, sticking a Diaklave in her back is <i>very</i> satisfying.<br /> <br /> And <i>then</i> you get to take her stuff!<br /> <br /> Like, obviously the Night Cast could have used Athletics Charms to get up there, but they don't know Raksi's statline in-character! That's OOC knowledge; my players aren't metagaming scum! All they knew was she was some kind of bad-ass Lunar elder and as newly-reborn Solars they should fight her as a team or not at all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T14:01:06-07:00","id":286906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286814#post286814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was your takeaway about Raksi then the write-up failed miserably.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe I'm just too firmly lodged in my 21st century Western morality here, but I think eating babies is a fairly safe indication that someone's evil, or a more morally neutral term that has every one of the same connotations. It's a radical notion, I know, that maybe disqualifies me from truly understanding the world of Exalted, but I'm sticking to it. I read those excerpts and thought of the NAMBLA episode of South Park, where Stan rebuts every eloquent argument with &quot;Dude....you have sex with KIDS!&quot;<br /> <br /> More to the point, I wouldn't expect my players to react to that revelation with anything other than &quot;Kill.&quot;, and I can't think of any moral counter-argument about why they shouldn't have that reaction. One fan suggestion I really liked to make Raksi actually usable as more than a raid boss, was that she had actually perfectly memorised and then destroyed the Book of Three Circles, such that the possibly irreplacable knowledge of Solar Sorcery dies when she does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T14:03:07-07:00","id":286908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286893#post286893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And more importantly, with the unambiguously evil Raksi narrative I ran with, my players had <i>hella </i><i>fun</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually glad you had fun, but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286893#post286893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You remember <i>fun </i>don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno what you think you're going to accomplish in a discussion when you make childish, trollish comments like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T14:12:16-07:00","id":286913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286904#post286904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This problem is solved with <i>very basic </i>encounter design.</div> </div> </div> </div>...It's really not.<br /> I <b>guess</b> you could stack the deck with 2nd circle demons but then the achievement is defeating them rather than Raksi.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-19-2014, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T14:20:25-07:00","id":286920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286913#post286913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...It's really not.<br /> I <b>guess</b> you could stack the deck with 2nd circle demons but then the achievement is defeating them rather than Raksi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creatures a summoner can summon are absolutely a facet of her powers and training and don't let any greatsword-wielding muscle-head tell you any different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T14:23:08-07:00","id":286922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286904#post286904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, obviously the Night Cast could have used Athletics Charms to get up there, but they don't know Raksi's statline in-character! That's OOC knowledge; my players aren't metagaming scum! All they knew was she was some kind of bad-ass Lunar elder and as newly-reborn Solars they should fight her as a team or not at all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides, if he'd tried that, he'd have found a Lunar elder with all DBT upgrades, Dexterity 10 and bad touch Speed 3 attacks.<br /> <br /> I mean why would Raksi ever use <i>spells</i> when she has a giant monster form that gets to use Principle of Motion, that's just a waste of motes. But I guess that, as always happens in NPC write-ups, her write-up fails to include some basic Charm that serves as a cornerstone of Exalted survivability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T15:05:01-07:00","id":286947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286908#post286908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm actually glad you had fun, but...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I dunno what you think you're going to accomplish in a discussion when you make childish, trollish comments like this.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I am not trolling you, I am seriously concerned because prioritizing a nuanced, mature, complex setting over a setting that's actually fun to play in ruined 2e as much as it's clunky combat and diplomacy mechanics did.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This kind of prioritizing is the reason the Bronze Faction seems unambiguously right about the Solars in 2e, why the Realm's &quot;White Man's Burden&quot;-type excuses for it's behavior are actually taken seriously by the writing, it's the reason there's a brothel in the 2e Underworld filled with the polymorphed ghosts of rapists who, as punishment, are </span></span></span><i>themselves raped</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and the text implicitly treats this as a form of </span></span></span><i>just punishment.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So, you'll forgive me if I'm a bit </span></span></span><i>crass</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> when it comes to this mindset. Shit ain't always gotta be complex. Sometimes the returning heroes from an Age long past are </span></span></span><i>actually heroes </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">and not the inevitable bringers of the apocolypse</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. Sometimes the evil empire is </span></span></span><i>actually an evil empire</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and not a benevolent bringer of infrastructure, education, and medicine</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Fucking </span></span></span><i>rape is always bad</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> using it as a punishment for rape isn't a point in favor for the complexity and maturity of the setting, it's just something <i>else</i> I have to awkwardly explain to potential players that it </span></span></span>exists in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Complexity is stupid and unhelpful when implies the baby-eating, civilization-destroying, Wyld-tainted evil witch is actually what the setting considers a positive force in Creation so your PCs shouldn't try to defeat her; in fact, according to some text, she exists primarily to potential mentor for a PC sorcerer instead of an evil to be vanquished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T15:18:10-07:00","id":286951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286947#post286947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I am not trolling you, I am seriously concerned because prioritizing a nuanced, mature, complex setting over a setting that's actually fun to play in ruined 2e as much as it's clunky combat and diplomacy mechanics did.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This kind of prioritizing is the reason the Bronze Faction seems unambiguously right about the Solars in 2e, why the Realm's &quot;White Man's Burden&quot;-type excuses for it's behavior are actually taken seriously by the writing, it's the reason there's a brothel in the 2e Underworld filled with the polymorphed ghosts of rapists who, as punishment, are </span></span></span><i>themselves raped</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and the text implicitly treats this as a form of </span></span></span><i>just punishment.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Those things don't sound very complex and mature to me. <i>Maybe </i>it was a problem with the execution, rather than the goal?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T16:54:39-07:00","id":286997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286951#post286951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those things don't sound very complex and mature to me. <i>Maybe </i>it was a problem with the execution, rather than the goal?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you'll read the post you quoted one more time, you will see that I didn't say the <i>goal </i>of having a complex an nuanced setting was bad; that's what people play Exalted for. What I'm saying is if you prioritize having mature and complex setting over having a setting that's actually fun to play in... well, there you go; the setting itself won't be fun to play in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:02:42-07:00","id":287006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286845#post286845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You... kinda do unless you're a Scavenger Lord. Entering a dungeon without some kind of <i>goal</i> just feels clumsy and gamey; it breaks your immersion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then be a Scavenger Lord. It's not like anything is stopping you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And furthermore, questionable ethical outcomes? About killing Raksi? There are none; she's a threat to civilized peoples everywhere (and my PCs were, if nothing else, champions of civilization, so it worked in <i>my </i>campaign) and literally kiddnaps and <i>eats babies.</i> You've done Creation a favor by freeing up her Exaltation for a new, less diabolical host.<br /> <br /> If you want a <i>really evil fucker</i> for your PCs to kill in the Southeast, Raksi is perfect the way she is. </div> </div> </div>Bad writing is bad. Also, you may strategically screw yourself over in freeing the hand of others even worse. While not righteous, it is a blunder even greater than slaying an unjust ruler and said ruler's attendant cronies, only for the populace to subsequently starve en masse because there's no more grain distribution system. If you're going to do this, at least acknowledge that there has to be more done than going around lopping off heads.<br /> <br /> Edit: By some happenstance, you may read that as &quot;don't deal with Raksi&quot;. This is not the case. There is often an order of operations that can make dealing with challenges much easier, and crawling typically doesn't accomplish that. Perhaps it doesn't have the satisfaction of immediate &quot;righteous&quot; action, but playing with others' buttons can probably get a few headaches out of the way, like the aforementioned grain distribution issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-19-2014, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:12:39-07:00","id":287009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287006#post287006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then be a Scavenger Lord. It's not like anything is stopping you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bad writing is bad. Also, you may strategically screw yourself over in freeing the hand of others even worse. While not righteous, it is a blunder even greater than slaying an unjust ruler and said ruler's attendant cronies, only for the populace to subsequently starve en masse because there's no more grain distribution system. If you're going to do this, at least acknowledge that there has to be more done than going around lopping off heads.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if your campaign isn't <i>about</i> being a Scavenger Lord? Most Exalted campaigns <i>aren't.</i><br /> <br /> Government generally does at lot less than you seem think it does; do you think grain in Creation is generally distributed by governments benevolently looking out for the well-being of their people for merchants looking to sell it at a profit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:20:03-07:00","id":287011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287009#post287009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Government generally does at lot less than you seem think it does; farmers usually don't <i>stop farming</i> because of a regime change. Grain is generally distributed by merchants who want to sell it for profit, not governments benevolently looking out for the best interests of their people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Governmental collapse or radical change (as in, 'the kingdom falls,' not 'a new king replaces the previous one' is historically usually followed by dramatic changes in agricultural practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:30:23-07:00","id":287020,"title":"","content":"This is true, but stable occupation by a foreign power isn't &quot;collapse&quot; (especially with Tiger Warriors and 2e Eclipse Caste charms). Did Raksi even have a &quot;state&quot;? This campaign happened a long time ago; I can't remember. Is this discussion even applicable? I was under the impression Raksi just bullied all the tribes nearby her lair to pay her tribute and obey her and wasn't really involved in the day-to-day practice of statesmanship (or what passes for it in her territory.)<br /> <br /> ...also, incidentally, what's the PC term for a female statesman? Is it still statesman? Stateswoman?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:30:38-07:00","id":287021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287009#post287009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What if your campaign isn't <i>about</i> being a Scavenger Lord? Most Exalted campaigns <i>aren't.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Just the ones that you seem to be interested in. What do you think the main reason for dungeon crawling is in a setting where heroes don't get stronger by beating up random &quot;monsters&quot;? The only reason you would go to a bunch of scary ruins is to find something valuable enough to sell, and hopefully not so valuable that someone powerful gets interested. Of course, if you're powerful yourself, a whole new market just opened up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Government generally does at lot less than you seem think it does; do you think grain in Creation is generally distributed by governments benevolently looking out for the well-being of their people for merchants looking to sell it at a profit? </div> </div> </div>Government lets you know which people are on top. In the event that this becomes disputed, you can get quite a number of different people all trying to run the same thing. And by run, I mean control like a gang boss. And when there's an open internal struggle for power, food is going to get seized for said struggle, which doesn't leave the farmers in a good way, especially if their fields get burned or fouled by someone trying to cut the Gordian knot of territory struggles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:36:22-07:00","id":287025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287021#post287021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just the ones that you seem to be interested in. What do you think the main reason for dungeon crawling is in a setting where heroes don't get stronger by beating up random &quot;monsters&quot;? The only reason you would go to a bunch of scary ruins is to find something valuable enough to sell, and hopefully not so valuable that someone powerful gets interested. Of course, if you're powerful yourself, a whole new market just opened up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... maybe because whatever is in there is an evil, diabolical supervillian who needs to be put down before something disastrous happens? PCs don't enter dungeons to get loot (that's a nice motivator OOC, but it's not why the PCs, themselves, enter a dungeon) they usually do so as part of an ongoing mission or quest. Also, even in Exalted, dungeons still make you stronger if you find hearthstones, warstriders, Dire Lances or something similar in them. (My PCs found a few Hearthstones and a really sweet shawl-artifact for the Twilight caste; I forget what it did though. That certainly made them stronger.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287021#post287021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Government lets you know which people are on top. In the event that this becomes disputed, you can get quite a number of different people all trying to run the same thing. And by run, I mean control like a gang boss. And when there's an open internal struggle for power, food is going to get seized for said struggle, which doesn't leave the farmers in a good way, especially if their fields get burned or fouled by someone trying to cut the Gordian knot of territory struggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if you occupy the kingdom (or non-kingdom, non-state Lunar tribal authority) in question with your army, it is pretty apparent who is in charge now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:45:31-07:00","id":287032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286920#post286920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creatures a summoner can summon are absolutely a facet of her powers and training and don't let any greatsword-wielding muscle-head tell you any different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ordinarily yes.<br /> Though for Exalted NPCs that's less cut and dry, because they don't really do the summoning and just have whatever resources the ST deems appropriate to hand.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T17:57:55-07:00","id":287036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287032#post287032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ordinarily yes.<br /> Though for Exalted NPCs that's less cut and dry, because they don't really do the summoning and just have whatever resources the ST deems appropriate to hand.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This still doesn't make the encounter any less satisfying. You are aware you are only having to fight these Infernal things because of <i>Raksi's </i>power as a Celestial Circle Sorcerer. And even if you forget she's up on that balcony insulting you and reminding you what a great demonologist she is and how you <i>pale</i> in comparison to the might of <i>her</i> minions <i>she</i> summoned to destroy your <i>pathetic</i> Circle. This kind of fight can be just as entertaining and satisfying as a fight with a Stabby McDiaklave-style super villain.<br /> <br /> Encounter design, encounter design, e<i>ncounter design. </i>It cannot be stressed enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:02:30-07:00","id":287050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287025#post287025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh... maybe because whatever is in there is an evil, diabolical supervillian who needs to be put down before something disastrous happens? PCs don't enter dungeons to get loot (that's a nice motivator OOC, but it's not why the PCs, themselves, enter a dungeon) they usually do so as part of an ongoing mission or quest. Also, even in Exalted, dungeons still make you stronger if you find hearthstones, warstriders, Dire Lances or something similar in them. (My PCs found a few Hearthstones and a really sweet shawl-artifact for the Twilight caste; I forget what it did though. That certainly made them stronger.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're finding diabolical supervillains in the setting, it's probably evidence that a large number of setting concerns need work. Also, even if you keep the stuff, you're still a Scavenger Lord by any other name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, if you occupy the kingdom (or non-kingdom, non-state Lunar tribal authority) in question with your army, it is pretty apparent who is in charge now. </div> </div> </div>You do know what happens during military occupations, right? And the temptations that come with it at every level of organization?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:14:55-07:00","id":287052,"title":"","content":"Exalted supports the Solars being heroic returning god-kings who scour the land of various evils while amassing fame and fortune.<br /> <br /> It's fine to have villains that are simply villainous, and PCs that are mostly heroic. While some may think it adds something for the ST to say, &quot;By the way, the army you've created is happily raping and pillaging now because this is serious, realistic storytelling,&quot; others may not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:17:12-07:00","id":287053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287050#post287050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're finding diabolical supervillains in the setting, it's probably evidence that a large number of setting concerns need work. Also, even if you keep the stuff, you're still a Scavenger Lord by any other name.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are going to be extremely disappointed with any RPG you play if you don't want to find diabolical super villains. Exalted, in particular, is full of them. Keeping loot doesn't make you a Scavenger Lord, entering a dungeon with the sole in-character motivation for <i>loot</i> and/or <i>adventure </i>makes you a Scavenger Lord. What hero finds benign items that help him achieve his heroic goals and then decides to <i>not use them?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287050#post287050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know what happens during military occupations, right? And the temptations that come with it at every level of organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do know what happens in <i>governments</i>, right? And the temptations that come with it at every level of organization? And I mean damn, dude, what do you think Exalted is even <i>about</i>? I'm not saying corruption in an occupation government isn't a <i>problem, </i>but it's not enough of one to simply not ever <i>conquer stuff</i>. Man, what do you even think Exalted is about? This isn't &quot;Eclipse Caste the RPG&quot;; you're making it out like forceful or military options in Exalted <i>aren't useful </i>and that's <i>completely inconsistent with the setting.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:33:29-07:00","id":287066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287053#post287053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are going to be extremely disappointed with any RPG you play if you don't want to find diabolical super villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're fired. I don't even know how you got the job, but you're fired.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I've played RPGs, and not wanted &quot;diabolical super villains,&quot; and surprise surprise, <i>I got what I wanted.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-19-2014, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:46:10-07:00","id":287071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287066#post287066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're fired. I don't even know how you got the job, but you're fired.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I've played RPGs, and not wanted &quot;diabolical super villains,&quot; and surprise surprise, <i>I got what I wanted.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't work for you, inexplicably angry forum-goer! You don't own me!<br /> <br /> What <i>setting </i>though? Certainly not Exalted.<br /> <br /> Like, <i>campaigns </i>might not have diabolical super villains, but I can't think of an RPG <i>setting</i> that completely lacks them.<br /> <br /> I've only played World of Darkness, Exalted, Pathfinder, Dark Heresy, Only War, and Iron Kingdoms, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: AND Cthulu-Tech! I forgot about that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:48:10-07:00","id":287073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287036#post287036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This still doesn't make the encounter any less satisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable.<br /> NPCs don't follow the same rules as the PCs, that is an accepted fact, but when it feels like one may has <i>cheated</i> it's a reminder that success or failure is ultimately arbitrary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T18:59:36-07:00","id":287080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287073#post287073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Debatable.<br /> NPCs don't follow the same rules as the PCs, that is an accepted fact, but when it feels like one may has <i>cheated</i> it's a reminder that success or failure is ultimately arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's no accounting for taste I guess.<br /> <br /> You can mitigate the arbitrary feel of success/failure in an Exalted campaign by passing out a campaign guide for your players in Session Zero telling the party what skills will need to be covered and in heavy use*.<br /> <br /> If you feel like you've been <i>cheated </i>in a fight it's probably because of 2e's crappy combat system OR bad <i>encounter design</i>; I've found no class of enemy (except when Shaping Combat is involved, I <i>hate that shit)</i> in Exalted that is <i>innately</i> frustrating to fight, rock/paper/scissors nature of some Charm Trees excluded, of course.<br /> <br /> Are you sensing a pattern here?<br /> <br /> *If you're a methodical ST like me and not a more free-form one like the Storyteller System encourages you to be. I write up most of the content for my campaigns before the first session starts, so a player's guide is easy to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T19:55:16-07:00","id":287141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286997#post286997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you'll read the post you quoted one more time, you will see that I didn't say the <i>goal </i>of having a complex an nuanced setting was bad; that's what people play Exalted for. What I'm saying is if you prioritize having mature and complex setting over having a setting that's actually fun to play in... well, there you go; the setting itself won't be fun to play in.</div> </div> </div> </div>This still doesn't really follow from the examples you gave, though. The decision of whether or not to have the Ironic Punishment Rape Brothel is not whether you value a complex, mature setting over a playable one. On the whole, I'm hard-pressed to come up with an example where I think the two things are actually at odds in the game material. Exalted often fails at being playable and it often fails at being mature and complex but it isn't typically because of the competition between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T20:15:48-07:00","id":287176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287141#post287141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This still doesn't really follow from the examples you gave, though. The decision of whether or not to have the Ironic Punishment Rape Brothel is not whether you value a complex, mature setting over a playable one. On the whole, I'm hard-pressed to come up with an example where I think the two things are actually at odds in the game material. Exalted often fails at being playable and it often fails at being mature and complex but it isn't typically because of the competition between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, example;<br /> <br /> Empires improve territory they conquer only so they can more efficiently extract resources from those areas. This is a common trope with a lot of historical background:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=alJaltUmrGo\" data-code=\"alJaltUmrGo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/alJaltUmrGo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The Realm, as portrayed by some writers, is actually as benevolent as it's propaganda would lead you to believe. This is presented as a clever, nuanced subversion of the evil empire trope, for sure, but it's unhelpful when your primary PC splat is considered Anathema to the Realm. It's not fun and is in fact <i>quite frustrating </i>if stopping the Empire that is ruthlessly hunting you down and obstructing the Mandate of Heaven means ruining <i>everything for everyone </i>when you finally win. The entire story of new Solar kingdoms rising, forming alliances and marching on the Blessed Isle to <i>restore Celestial Law</i> is <i>ruined</i> if the Dynasts are actually the good guys.<br /> <br /> This trope was subverted in parts 2e to show how &quot;the truth defies simplicity&quot; which is all well and good, but if it invalidates the major themes of Solar campaigns then that added complexity comes at the expense of playability.<br /> <br /> We were talking about Lunar Elders before this thread got derailed, yes? I will continue my defense if my STing style and portrayal of Raksi in the campaign I ran years ago from the Forum's criticism if you wish (I can do this <i>for days)</i>, but you <i>can</i> go back to talking about Lunars if you want; I won't think less of you or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-19-2014, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T20:26:35-07:00","id":287183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287071#post287071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: AND Cthulu-Tech! I forgot about that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>DOUBLE FIRED!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T20:36:00-07:00","id":287197,"title":"","content":"Widespread turmoil resulting from the collapse of the Realm is good thing, even if you're running a game about nice, modern-sense heroic Solars.<br /> <br /> Hell, <i>especially</i> if you're running such a game. Here's your chance to prove your virtue, truly and absolutely, and do what no one's done before: clean up your own mess, and forge the Golden Age in righteousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T20:39:17-07:00","id":287198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287197#post287197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Widespread turmoil resulting from the collapse of the Realm is good thing, even if you're running a game about nice, modern-sense heroic Solars.<br /> <br /> Hell, <i>especially</i> if you're running such a game. Here's your chance to prove your virtue, truly and absolutely, and do what no one's done before: clean up your own mess, and forge the Golden Age in righteousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Collapse is good, fallout is good, consequences are good.<br /> <br /> Your Solar conquering the Realm being a <i>net negative</i> for Creation in the long run is not. It should be important for the Solars to replace the Realm not simply because <i>they want power</i> it should be because the Realm is corrupt and exploitative and the people <i>need </i>their Lawgivers once again.<br /> <br /> This should be the Empire that you, as a player, have real motivation to replace or reform because it's oppressive and self-serving in all its conquests, laws, governance and even religious practices.<br /> <br /> The theme we're going for here is &quot;Radiant hero-king reborn saves with world from tyranny and oppression&quot; not &quot;Glowy warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever.&quot; Exalted can certainly tell the latter story, but it's far from the default assumption for Solar campaigns and usually a sign that you dun goofed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-20-2014, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:30:24-07:00","id":287242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The empire that, until quite recently, controlled the whole of civilized Creation. Also called the Scarlet Empire, the Realm never officially &quot;ruled&quot; more than the Blessed Isle directly, but it exacted tribute from countless local governments, which paid it homage. Those governments were independent in theory, but they were actually little more than puppet states. <br /> <br /> Since the Scarlet Empress has disappeared, the Realm has been paralyzed by indecision. There is a weak Regent on the Scarlet Throne, and the various Houses of the Scarlet Dynasty plot endlessly, each attempting to gain enough power to place its own candidate on the Throne.<br /> <br /> In this Time of Tumult, many of the Realm's tributaries have had their garrisons recalled and been left to their own devices. While some remain loyal vassal states, a few have openly declared their independence. Many more have effectively done so quietly, withholding their tribute under flimsy excuses. Whoever takes the Throne will be faced with the monumental task of re-conquering a majority of the Realm's old territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts are: &quot;The Realm&quot; is now more of an ideal than a government. Instead, there are various Houses, Tributary states, and lesser factions that mostly go through the motions of, &quot;no, we're totally the same nation, really!&quot;, while actually doing things how <i>they</i> think they should be done.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the various factions would come in all colors, textures, flavors, and combinations of good, bad, and ugly.<br /> <br /> Deciding to &quot;save&quot; the Realm is almost <i>always</i> a morally acceptable choice if you can manage it, because if you <i>do</i> &quot;save&quot; it, what comes out will be what <i>you</i> make of it, not a constant. Even if you back one of the pre-existing factions, it's one that <i>you</i> chose, and probably will wield significant influence over, and thus presumably one that fits with your morals and standards.<br /> <br /> So, basically, the Realm isn't good or bad, it's fictional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4100-powerofvoid","name":"powerofvoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4100_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:31:54-07:00","id":287244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287198#post287198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theme we're going for here is &quot;Radiant hero-king reborn saves with world from tyranny and oppression&quot; not &quot;Glowy warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever.&quot; Exalted can certainly tell the latter story, but it's far from the default assumption for Solar campaigns and usually a sign that you dun goofed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not <i>the</i> default assumption, but it's one of them. The Lawgivers are consistently presented as the ones who might save or doom Creation, and each outcome is equally important.<br /> <br /> Besides, fucking everything up can be fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:37:30-07:00","id":287247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287198#post287198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Collapse is good, fallout is good, consequences are good.<br /> <br /> Your Solar conquering the Realm being a <i>net negative</i> for Creation in the long run is not. It should be important for the Solars to replace the Realm not simply because <i>they want power</i> it should be because the Realm is corrupt and exploitative and the people <i>need </i>their Lawgivers once again.<br /> <br /> This should be the Empire that you, as a player, have real motivation to replace or reform because it's oppressive and self-serving in all its conquests, laws, governance and even religious practices.<br /> <br /> The theme we're going for here is &quot;Radiant hero-king reborn saves with world from tyranny and oppression&quot; not &quot;Glowy warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever.&quot; Exalted can certainly tell the latter story, but it's far from the default assumption for Solar campaigns and usually a sign that you dun goofed.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that, while I am defending this campaign style <i>to the death</i> I'd much rather be the woods doing ranger things when I play a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Empire should not be depicted as a total evil empire. It should be depicted like an actual empire. They have all done good and bad. Often done bad for the sake of good. Political structures and entities are complex, morally grey things. Sure to the oppressed satrap they might seem kinda evil, but that same Empire protects them and regulates the metaphysical, which is a big deal in Exalted. The Empire is also not likely bad for the citizens of the Blessed Isle, prosperity and security the Empire provides. A political entity should never be irredeemably evil in Exalted.<br /> <br /> I also disagree with your theme. I'd argue it's &quot;Radiant hero-king reborn returns to change the world as they see fit.&quot; Be it good or ill is up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T23:46:46-07:00","id":287313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287198#post287198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Collapse is good, fallout is good, consequences are good.<br /> <br /> Your Solar conquering the Realm being a <i>net negative</i> for Creation in the long run is not. It should be important for the Solars to replace the Realm not simply because <i>they want power</i> it should be because the Realm is corrupt and exploitative and the people <i>need </i>their Lawgivers once again.<br /> <br /> This should be the Empire that you, as a player, have real motivation to replace or reform because it's oppressive and self-serving in all its conquests, laws, governance and even religious practices.<br /> <br /> The theme we're going for here is &quot;Radiant hero-king reborn saves with world from tyranny and oppression&quot; not &quot;Glowy warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever.&quot; Exalted can certainly tell the latter story, but it's far from the default assumption for Solar campaigns and usually a sign that you dun goofed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like it would create serious issues when the DB book has to be written, which has the default assumption of DBs working for the Realm unironically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T00:58:09-07:00","id":287332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287313#post287313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like it would create serious issues when the DB book has to be written, which has the default assumption of DBs working for the Realm unironically.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Working for the Realm&quot; doesn't (and shouldn't) mean &quot;mindlessly attempting to keep the Realm exactly as it is right now with no changes.&quot;<br /> <br /> In fact, the game is designed to make that goal nearly impossible -- while I suppose you technically <i>could</i> run a DB game where your goal is to recover the Empress, banish or imprison all the Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals forever, and permanently lock the Alchemicals out of Creation, I don't think that that is meant to be a feasible or, necessarily, desirable goal, and it absolutely is not the default goal for DB PCs.<br /> <br /> The default setting is meant to be an era of change, for the Realm more than any thing else. This setup gives your DB the possibility to make decisions that will shape the direction of that change.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a &quot;crusading DB of the Realm&quot; kind of game (without the shadow of the fact that the Realm-as-it-was is irrevocably doomed and must transform into something new to survive), you'd be better off setting it before the Jade Prison breaks and the Empress vanishes (or even saying it never does.) The default assumption for the game is that the Realm as it was for the past 700 years is irrevocably gone and cannot reasonably be precisely restored, with your character (whether you are a DB or something else) taking part in the fight over what exactly will replace it. As a Realm DB you can (and, yeah, often would be assumed to) fight for <i>some form</i> of Realm and some form of DB hegemony, but &quot;let's keep things exactly the way they were before&quot; is not meant to be a reasonable decision, and the game is set five years after the Empress vanished (rather than five minutes) precisely in order to ensure that it's at the point where most DBs are starting to realize that the old system is probably gone forever.<br /> <br /> I mean, Exalted allows you to play unreasonable stories, and it doesn't actually break the game to run a DB story where the Empress returns and puts everything the way it was before, but... it's not the default narrative, even for DBs. In <i>some ways</i>, making it the default narrative would have the same problems that the Reclamation did (namely, focusing heavily on returning the Empress and basically rolling back the clock on the past five years requires overriding the significance of everything else in the setting.) It's not quite so bad, because it works with elements that are meant to be central, but I don't think it's healthy for the game to encourage DB players to view &quot;put things exactly the way they were before&quot; as their default goal, unless they do it with the understanding that it can only be accomplished imperfectly (and therefore that they're really going to be creating something new.)<br /> <br /> Trying to maintain the aspects of the Realm you think are good? Trying to recreate the old order of the Realm on your own terms under a new system? Those things are cool. But that means that you're, ultimately, replacing or reforming the Realm-as-it-was, at least in some ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-11-2015, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T02:39:40-07:00","id":287369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287176#post287176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were talking about Lunar Elders before this thread got derailed, yes? I will continue my defense if my STing style and portrayal of Raksi in the campaign I ran years ago from the Forum's criticism if you wish (I can do this <i>for days)</i>, but you <i>can</i> go back to talking about Lunars if you want; I won't think less of you or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your Storytelling style is currently more interesting to people than a dead horse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T03:14:03-07:00","id":287383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286850#post286850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, this is still fun.<br /> Writers who didn't do their homework into where Gary Gygax got his ideas from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am intruiged, but do not understand! Where did Gygax get his idea from? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T03:44:53-07:00","id":287411,"title":"","content":"The backwards hands of the Dungeons and Dragons Rakshasa draw their origins from the TV series Kolchak: The Night Stalker, specifically the episode Horror in the Heights.<br /> It's a fun watch if you've got time (or an excuse to study television history like I did) and want to see what also inspired the X-files.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T04:01:49-07:00","id":287438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287411#post287411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The backwards hands of the Dungeons and Dragons Rakshasa draw their origins from the TV series Kolchak: The Night Stalker, specifically the episode Horror in the Heights.<br /> It's a fun watch if you've got time (or an excuse to study television history like I did) and want to see what also inspired the X-files.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is actually Exactley what I might have a reason to do right now. Haha. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","user":"Kim","date":". 10-20-2014, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T05:18:20-07:00","id":287490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286947#post286947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Complexity is stupid and unhelpful when implies the baby-eating, civilization-destroying, Wyld-tainted evil witch is actually what the setting considers a positive force in Creation</div> </div> </div> </div>Those details should be changed.<br /> <br /> Making a big deal out of characters who would not be out of place as the villains of pot-boiler murder mystery novels is not a good thing, regardless of their potential to give players happy power trips.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean Raksi can't be a person who does terrible things, but at least put it in a context akin to looking on Genghis Khan from the perspective of somebody on the European frontier or the Central Asian steppes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T05:33:09-07:00","id":287500,"title":"","content":"As for Solars as fairly straightforward heroes, when I picture Demetheus taking on a whole bunch of bad guys from the South, I see the matter is unambiguous mostly because they're greedy and selfish rather than because they go in for extravagant and elaborate displays of evil.<br /> <br /> Heck, not even all of that; I think it's perfectly valid for one Exalt to fight another who's something of a terrorist, well-intentioned but using extreme methods, which may or may not end up in killing them, and still follow the basic course of heroism (even if it would help that they then try to work on the thing the other person was fighting for). Complementary motivations can still be a compelling basis of conflict without it needing to overdo a sense of political realism, if one character's motivations are enabled by activities within certain social systems that have harmful impacts on other people, and the other one is a lone kung-fu action hero.<br /> <br /> And then there are antagonists who are lone kung-fu action villains, as in they're also going around getting into fights with other powerful figures in order to determine who's the strongest, just a lot more extreme about it, and generally kind of an asshole.<br /> <br /> My point is, making the context in which a character like Raksi exists more complex doesn't need to mean that all interactions with her are (although there can be matters of presentation that define whether some are righteous or thuggish).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:04:45-07:00","id":287574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287244#post287244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not <i>the</i> default assumption, but it's one of them. The Lawgivers are consistently presented as the ones who might save or doom Creation, and each outcome is equally important.<br /> <br /> Besides, fucking everything up can be fun too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the context here made my meaning clear, but if it wasn't I will specify:<br /> <br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because the Great Curse made the same as the tyrants he sought to usurp</b>&quot;is not destructive to the themes of the Solar Exalted, as a PC, the Great Curse is just more epic adversity you have to overcome, and that's a <i>good thing </i>for a Solar-centered narrative.<br /> <br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because the Realm didn't need to be replaced or reformed in the first place</b>&quot; makes in unambiguously clear that Solar PCs are not supposed to be protagonists. Solars are supposed to be the Heroes of this story and if they fail they fail because they were insufficient to the task, not because the people of the setting<b> didn't need any help to begin with.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-20-2014, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:13:28-07:00","id":287586,"title":"","content":"I'm a little lost - where did we make the jump from &quot;Villains in Exalted, both of the human and institutional variety, don't need to be unambiguously evil&quot; to &quot;Anyone (especially Solars) trying to help the world by defeating villains is only making things worse for everyone&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:18:40-07:00","id":287590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287586#post287586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little lost - where did we make the jump from &quot;Villains in Exalted, both of the human and institutional variety, don't need to be unambiguously evil&quot; to &quot;Anyone (especially Solars) trying to help the world by defeating villains is only making things worse for everyone&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the same issue: &quot;sacrificing playability for complexity&quot; which is what we're still talking about, <i>I think.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:27:50-07:00","id":287603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287574#post287574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the context here made my meaning clear, but if it wasn't I will specify:<br /> <br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because the Great Curse made the same as the tyrants he sought to usurp</b>&quot;is not destructive to the themes of the Solar Exalted, as a PC, the Great Curse is just more epic adversity you have to overcome, and that's a <i>good thing </i>for a Solar-centered narrative.<br /> <br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because the Realm didn't need to be replaced or reformed in the first place</b>&quot; makes in unambiguously clear that Solar PCs are not supposed to be protagonists. Solars are supposed to be the Heroes of this story and if they fail they fail because they were insufficient to the task, not because the people of the setting<b> didn't need any help to begin with.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, moral ambiguity! It might make me consider the consequences of my actions! It might mean I'm not acting from an unambiguous moral high ground! Nuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu~!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:43:01-07:00","id":287613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287603#post287603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, moral ambiguity! It might make me consider the consequences of my actions! It might mean I'm not acting from an unambiguous moral high ground! Nuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu~!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm talking about at all. I'm not saying there shouldn't be a moral grey area, I'm saying if the Realm is presented in the text as the <b>unambiguous good guys</b> it makes the Solars the <b>unambiguous bad guys</b> if they try to do anything about the current state of Creation and that makes the setting unplayable for Solar protagonists.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:43:13-07:00","id":287614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287071#post287071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't work for you, inexplicably angry forum-goer!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not angry, believe you me. I'll let you know when that happens.<br /> <br /> Now, you <i>say</i> you don't work for me, you say I don't own you\u2026 and I certainly don't belong to or work for <i>you</i>\u2026 so with these being the case, what makes you think you get to say what will or won't disappoint me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What <i>setting </i>though? Certainly not Exalted. </div> </div> </div>Certainly Exalted. It's pretty easy to run or play Exalted without one-note diabolical supervillains, in fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, <i>campaigns </i>might not have diabolical super villains, but I can't think of an RPG <i>setting</i> that completely lacks them. </div> </div> </div>I don't make the distinction, myself. A setting with no campaigns is less than useless, not even trash. Even FATAL has had at least one game of it played. Settings are written for games, and games are set somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've only played World of Darkness, Exalted, Pathfinder, Dark Heresy, Only War, and Iron Kingdoms, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: AND Cthulu-Tech! I forgot about that one. </div> </div> </div>If you're playing or running games set in all of those, and <i>can't have a game bereft of diabolical supervillains</i>, I legitimately pity you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:48:28-07:00","id":287621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287614#post287614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I'm not angry, believe you me. I'll let you know when that happens.<br /> <br /> Now, you <i>say</i> you don't work for me, you say I don't own you\u2026 and I certainly don't belong to or work for <i>you</i>\u2026 so with these being the case, what makes you think you get to say what will or won't disappoint me?<br /> <br /> Certainly Exalted. It's pretty easy to run or play Exalted without one-note diabolical supervillains, in fact.<br /> <br /> I don't make the distinction, myself. A setting with no campaigns is less than useless, not even trash. Even FATAL has had at least one game of it played. Settings are written for games, and games are set somewhere.<br /> <br /> If you're playing or running games set in all of those, and <i>can't have a game bereft of diabolical supervillains</i>, I legitimately pity you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you payed attention to the post I was quoting you would have noticed we were talking about settings not campaigns:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287050#post287050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you're finding diabolical supervillains in the setting, it's probably evidence that a large number of setting concerns need work.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>All those settings (Iron Kingdoms, Exalted, Pathfinder, WoD, Cthulu-Tech, Dark Heresy, Only War) have diabolical super villains in them, even if your campaign decides to simply ignore them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-20-2014, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:52:44-07:00","id":287628,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't know what ya'll are talking about - in RPGs, I kill people who are only ambiguously evil all the time. I mess around with governments, too.<br /> <br /> Who here remembers Loghain, from Dragon Age: Origins? The guy betrays you during the prologue of the game by leaving the Grey Wardens to die along with the King, leaving the nation of Ferelden unable to mount a good defense against the Blight because the nobles who followed the King are split on following Loghain. At first, it's easy to assume that Loghain is just a bastard - his allies are mostly jerks (especially if you're playing a Human Noble, in which case his chief lieutenant killed your family), but on inspection it becomes apparent that he did what he did because he genuinely thought that the Grey Wardens were not that important to stopping the Blight (incorrect, but it's a mistake anyone who wasn't a Warden could make), and because he thought the King would sell out Ferelden to the neighboring country of Orlais, which Loghain had led a rebellion against decades earlier.<br /> <br /> Eventually, you can confront him, and kill him in a duel. I chose to kill him, not because I really believed he was a bad person and deserved to die for the good of everyone else, but because by the time I got to Loghain I had already killed a lot of people for much less serious crimes than Loghain's (Usually, for the crimes of attacking a Grey Warden, or banditry), and I wanted my ethics to be consistent.<br /> <br /> Still made for a decent boss fight, and one that gave me something to reflect on afterward.<br /> <br /> Then I set up a buddy of mine with Loghain's daughter/the Queen to the late King, so there would be a clear succession of leadership - somebody had to take charge, and it couldn't be me. My buddy wasn't much of a leader-type but he was likeable, and did have royal blood, while the Queen was a good administrator without enough popular support. I announced this spontaneously-arranged marriage without consulting either of them. Was that unambiguously good? No, probably not, but it was the best I could do at the time.<br /> <br /> When my actions have consequences beyond &quot;And then there was peace, in the absence of violence and tyranny&quot;, I tend to remember them better, and it's still fun for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:09:56-07:00","id":287643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287613#post287613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not what I'm talking about at all. I'm not saying there shouldn't be a moral grey area, I'm saying if the Realm is presented in the text as the <b>unambiguous good guys</b> it makes the Solars the <b>unambiguous bad guys</b> if they try to do anything about the current state of Creation and that makes the setting unplayable for Solar protagonists.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm has never been unambiguously good. The realm is a massive Creation spanning organization with thousands of Exalts dedicated to protecting and supporting it's citizenry, if for no oher reason than because of the practical concern of protecting their interests. The Realm is portrayed as doing a lot of bad things, but the Realm is also portrayed, unironically, as having protected Creation for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> Deciding to take down the Realm should be a big deal, not just for how to actually do so, but also for how to do so without Creation literally crumbling around you. I don't think this is a flaw, but rather a feature. As oft maligned as it is in Exalted discussions, TTGL is actually a a great example of this sort of things and is a good example of how I think this is intended to play out in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:10:06-07:00","id":287644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287628#post287628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't know what ya'll are talking about - in RPGs, I kill people who are only ambiguously evil all the time. I mess around with governments, too.<br /> <br /> Who here remembers Loghain, from Dragon Age: Origins? The guy betrays you during the prologue of the game by leaving the Grey Wardens to die along with the King, leaving the nation of Ferelden unable to mount a good defense against the Blight because the nobles who followed the King are split on following Loghain. At first, it's easy to assume that Loghain is just a bastard - his allies are mostly jerks (especially if you're playing a Human Noble, in which case his chief lieutenant killed your family), but on inspection it becomes apparent that he did what he did because he genuinely thought that the Grey Wardens were not that important to stopping the Blight (incorrect, but it's a mistake anyone who wasn't a Warden could make), and because he thought the King would sell out Ferelden to the neighboring country of Orlais, which Loghain had led a rebellion against decades earlier.<br /> <br /> Eventually, you can confront him, and kill him in a duel. I chose to kill him, not because I really believed he was a bad person and deserved to die for the good of everyone else, but because by the time I got to Loghain I had already killed a lot of people for much less serious crimes than Loghain's (Usually, for the crimes of attacking a Grey Warden, or banditry), and I wanted my ethics to be consistent.<br /> <br /> Still made for a decent boss fight, and one that gave me something to reflect on afterward.<br /> <br /> Then I set up a buddy of mine with Loghain's daughter/the Queen to the late King, so there would be a clear succession of leadership - somebody had to take charge, and it couldn't be me. My buddy wasn't much of a leader-type but he was likeable, and did have royal blood, while the Queen was a good administrator without enough popular support. I announced this spontaneously-arranged marriage without consulting either of them. Was that unambiguously good? No, probably not, but it was the best I could do at the time.<br /> <br /> When my actions have consequences beyond &quot;And then there was peace, in the absence of violence and tyranny&quot;, I tend to remember them better, and it's still fun for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between this and what I'm talking about is while Loghain had his reasons it was <i>still</i> imperative he be removed from power. The 2e text on the Realm <b>constantly asserts </b>that the Realm is just <b>perfect </b>for the people of Creation as-is and the current system doesn't need changing <i>at all</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:16:30-07:00","id":287647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287574#post287574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the context here made my meaning clear, but if it wasn't I will specify:<br /> <br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because the Great Curse made the same as the tyrants he sought to usurp</b>&quot;is not destructive to the themes of the Solar Exalted, as a PC, the Great Curse is just more epic adversity you have to overcome, and that's a <i>good thing </i>for a Solar-centered narrative.<br /> <br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because the Realm didn't need to be replaced or reformed in the first place</b>&quot; makes in unambiguously clear that Solar PCs are not supposed to be protagonists. Solars are supposed to be the Heroes of this story and if they fail they fail because they were insufficient to the task, not because the people of the setting<b> didn't need any help to begin with.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because he wouldn't wait for the right moment to act.</b>&quot; Being a Solar doesn't keep you from having to plan and time campaigns correctly. You've got to play sides off one another to defuse a lot of high-stakes situations, and again, even Solar Exalted are subject to these limitations. Being Solars means that they can attempt great feats, but is no guarantee of their success or a shield from their consequences, and this is a consistent problem with the writing from late first edition through most of second edition. When it's not naming canon NPCs Tori Amos (spelled backwards), it's incredibly lazy about setting up potential conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:22:44-07:00","id":287655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287647#post287647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because he wouldn't wait for the right moment to act.</b>&quot; Being a Solar doesn't keep you from having to plan and time campaigns correctly. You've got to play sides off one another to defuse a lot of high-stakes situations, and again, even Solar Exalted are subject to these limitations. Being Solars means that they can attempt great feats, but is no guarantee of their success or a shield from their consequences, and this is a consistent problem with the writing from late first edition through most of second edition. When it's not naming canon NPCs Tori Amos (spelled backwards), it's incredibly lazy about setting up potential conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one way to portray Solars in-theme but I don't know why you've included my quote because it has nothing to do with what I was talking about in that post. at no point did I say (or even imply) <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Glowy Warmonger ruins everything for everyone ever <b>because he wouldn't wait for the right moment to act.</b>&quot; was invalid; I simply wasn't discussing that angle at all.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-20-2014, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:31:51-07:00","id":287664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287574#post287574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are supposed to be the Heroes of this story and if they fail they fail because they were insufficient to the task, not because the people of the setting<b> didn't need any help to begin with.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting this?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:42:23-07:00","id":287671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287176#post287176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, example;<br /> <br /> Empires improve territory they conquer only so they can more efficiently extract resources from those areas. This is a common trope with a lot of historical background:<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> The Realm, as portrayed by some writers, is actually as benevolent as it's propaganda would lead you to believe. This is presented as a clever, nuanced subversion of the evil empire trope, for sure, but it's unhelpful when your primary PC splat is considered Anathema to the Realm. It's not fun and is in fact <i>quite frustrating </i>if stopping the Empire that is ruthlessly hunting you down and obstructing the Mandate of Heaven means ruining <i>everything for everyone </i>when you finally win. The entire story of new Solar kingdoms rising, forming alliances and marching on the Blessed Isle to <i>restore Celestial Law</i> is <i>ruined</i> if the Dynasts are actually the good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is seeming to get into a couple weird issues. First, assuming that the Realm itself has to be good in order for people in it to be good (this is somewhat what the imperial apologists in other threads tend to do). Second, it assumes that it's bad that you as Solars don't inherently have some legitimacy to rulership by you not being the Realm. This second point kind of misses wha thas been talked about at length by devs in the idea that Solars are somewhat a subversion of the Destined Returned Hero. The White Rose coming back doens't mean shit if she can't acutally run things when she gets the job done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287176#post287176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This trope was subverted in parts 2e to show how &quot;the truth defies simplicity&quot; which is all well and good, but if it invalidates the major themes of Solar campaigns then that added complexity comes at the expense of playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an example of I think cherry-picking a bit. &quot;The Realm is actually good&quot; is often kind of argued as actually being in itself a simplification, as having a PC splat serve a full blown evil insitution would be bad times, afterall. So authors tried to rehabilitate the institution instead of let PCs have moral conflicts. You cite an example of attempts for nuance, and I think a lot of the detractors of the course see it as actualy being overly simplistic.<br /> <br /> It also is presenting a false dichotomy that playability is contrasted with nuance. Nuance to me adds story options and interesting consequences. If it's a forgone conclusion that I'm in the right, than there's not really a challenge to be had. The Realm doesn't need to be Evil or Villainous, but it is. And it being either of those doesn't mean it isn't simple, it's just that authors in 2e thought complexity was brought by showing how good the Realm is inherently, rather than the actuality of empires having &quot;good&quot; as peripheral side effect to things.<br /> <br /> The <i>Life of Brian</i> scene where &quot;What have the Romans ever done for us?&quot; is interesting in that despite all the things the Romans gave them, and there being many Jews at hte time who sided with it, there was still a big ass rebellion seventy years later, and just over a century and a half something so big the Romans went on full blown attempt ot genocide to make sure it didn't happen again. This is all while still building roads, aquaducts and police order. Similarly, as found in the novel <i>Thints Fall Apart</i>, murder over tribal grievances, letting twins to die via exposrue, or treating outcastes as people was something the British colonial government nad missionaries helped stop. At the price of destroying local customs, putting strain on religious beliefs in a region for centuries, and punishing people for crimes they did not understand or did not know could exist. <br /> <br /> Defeating the Realm shouldn't be easy not becuase the Realm is actually good and that makes your PCs feel bad. it shouldn't be easy because destroying local power structures isn't easy. The 2e writers just kind of fucked-up on doing that as it wasn't seeking naunce, but simplicity of &quot;Good versus bad&quot;. It wasn't thinking consequences, which is what I think good presentation of political upheaval should focus on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287176#post287176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were talking about Lunar Elders before this thread got derailed, yes? I will continue my defense if my STing style and portrayal of Raksi in the campaign I ran years ago from the Forum's criticism if you wish (I can do this <i>for days)</i>, but you <i>can</i> go back to talking about Lunars if you want; I won't think less of you or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Elders in 2e generlaly sucked. The issue folks have is not that you depicted Raksi that way. That's for your game. The issue si that for a lot of how Exalted is vaunted, 2e's portrayal of her was lazy, a tad stupid, and to top it off a bit on the creeper side in parts (which bled into her depiction in the OP's depiction I would note). <br /> <br /> Raksi in 1e, as a note, was a tad more subtle. She had influence on teh Ten Tribes for reasons we didn't know, and she seemed to be while a monsterous cannibal, much more in control of things than the 2e depiciton had. She wasn't some teen wtih daddy issues over millennia (for one she was never implied as to being a preteen when she Exalted). She was depicted giving a meeting for her troops and a patron to younger Lunars willing to put up with her shit. She's originally sort of a regional power, something you deal with to get power, and who if she died might actually cause issues, like that Thousand Fangs Army not having a head anymore.<br /> <br /> It was 2e's depiction that reduced her to a insular brat in a city of apemen with no hinted political savvy and who had no real even reason to have the Ten Tribes invovlement. 2e took what was potentially a neat wide-ranging mentor and power player and made her into something out of Saturday morning cartoons. Your depiction runs on that, as it appears, but it should be noted that your depiction of her is based on what is in essence lazy writing, nto simpler writing. And that it wasn't complex doesn't mean it dichotomously meant it had to be good. THey aren't some continuum from one-another or diometrically opposed as you seem to argue about.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T08:56:51-07:00","id":287681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287671#post287671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was 2e's depiction that reduced her to a insular brat in a city of apemen with no hinted political savvy and who had no real even reason to have the Ten Tribes invovlement. 2e took what was potentially a neat wide-ranging mentor and power player and made her into something out of Saturday morning cartoons. Your depiction runs on that, as it appears, but it should be noted that your depiction of her is based on what is in essence lazy writing, nto simpler writing. And that it wasn't complex doesn't mean it dichotomously meant it had to be good. THey aren't some continuum from one-another or diometrically opposed as you seem to argue about.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you're projecting and not actually reading my posts.<br /> <br /> Nowhere in this entire thread have I stated that complexity and playability are innately opposed to each other, what I've been saying this entire time (and explaining over and over and over) is that when complexity is <i>given priority </i>over playability then <i>playability suffers.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:19:53-07:00","id":287721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287681#post287681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like you're projecting and not actually reading my posts.<br /> <br /> Nowhere in this entire thread have I stated that complexity and playability are innately opposed to each other, what I've been saying this entire time (and explaining over and over and over) is that when complexity is <i>given priority </i>over playability then <i>playability suffers.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>However, your example (Good Guy Realm) is an example of simplicity, not complexity, as it attempted to remove ambiguity of PCs or the Realm's imperial state issues. And the parts about where you often detride others for not liking fun for liking complexity, seem to indicate that implictily if not explicitly you find authors should prioritize fun over complexity, whih often to the detriment of nuance in depictions of characters. Your praise of 2e Raksi and your depictions of her in game show this. She is not complex. And you have not seemed to show interest in making her more complex, as that threatens her playability.<br /> <br /> So while you claim your arguments show they can be compatable, the structures of your concerns and examples indicate more often a slide to them being opposed. Which is then why folks respond and criticize your points, as you have not actually argued well that you aren't presenting what many see as a false dichotomy.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:20:53-07:00","id":287722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287681#post287681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you're projecting and not actually reading my posts.<br /> <br /> Nowhere in this entire thread have I stated that complexity and playability are innately opposed to each other, what I've been saying this entire time (and explaining over and over and over) is that when complexity is <i>given priority </i>over playability then <i>playability suffers.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>No, the issue people are having is that you're assuming and asserting the problem was a matter of deliberately prioritizing complexity over playability. That such a prioritization happened can't even be inferred, here, because the actual problem was that what was written was not written very well.<br /> <br /> As people are trying to emphasize to you, the examples you have raised to support your position that &quot;prioritizing complex and nuance over playability is bad&quot; don't do so at all. This is because the examples you have raised fail very impressively at being complex and nuanced. If you're going to try to make your case, find better examples. The ones you've put forth give people cause to question whether you understand what they mean when they say they want complexity and nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:37:45-07:00","id":287750,"title":"","content":"A complex Realm is not one that doesn't need help, it's one that needs help more sophisticated than taking out the few bad apples so the rest of the cart can stay upright.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;killing this one villain and then striking a Conan pose doesn't make anything substantially better&quot; doesn't mean the villain was good, nor that it wasn't a decent thing to destroy them, it just means that the story doesn't end there.<br /> <br /> A similar thing can go with figures like Raksi; whatever she's like as a person, if killing her means that there's a power vacuum in the locality and the Silver Pact that Realm forces and other Lunar elders and various other figures try to fill, or the Silver Pact has a sudden deficit in power, or some of her own sorcerous insights are lost beyond recollection... well, depending on the type of character you're playing, that might give you pause in killing her, or want to set things up against the future in order to minimise the impact of her death, or even make a moral stand in saying &quot;whatever the other consequences, she's a terrible and dangerous person who needs to go down now&quot; doesn't mean she's actually secretly good, or that killing her is a bad thing. It doesn't even mean you can't go straight to that step, rather than have it come in at the ending. It just means that it won't be a matter of throwing her down the exhaust shaft, and then skip through a montage of scenes of everybody joyfully celebrating how they're instantly free and their lives have improved.<br /> <br /> Although even then, there doesn't necessarily have to be chaos. You can plausibly have it that, between the other things going on in the setting and some of the vagaries of chance, other forces don't get involved and the local situation settles down rather quietly. That's something I'd say happens if the game really doesn't want to stay in this place.<br /> <br /> But even that is at least acknowledging that there are bigger things to the setting, and how characters are thankful at the good fortune of having managed to dodge th worst of it.<br /> <br /> You'll hardly ever get a character who is so terrible that the Circle can smash them down with nary a twinge of conscience and also lacks any connection to anything else at all in the setting that there can't be bigger implications to their presence and absence.<br /> <br /> Even in cases where you do, where you've got somebody like Dio Brando, Akuma from Street Fighter, the Beast from Kung Fu Hustle or the bad guys from The Man With the Iron Fists... they should be there because they're compelling and fearsome, not rendered simplistic so that they can be easy targets.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't even take that tack towards roaming behemoths (or some of the smarter ones, like Arad the Hunter). If it was me, I'd approach them in terms of the Crystalline Entity from Star Trek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:46:17-07:00","id":287777,"title":"","content":"I think Lunar elders in general...<br /> <br /> I don't think they should necessarily be intrusive presences, or commander figures like Sidereal elders or the Deathlords, but I do think they should have a sense of presence and scope such that other Lunars are aware of at least the outlines of their plans, and it shapes their perception of the world. Like, even if Ma-Ha-Suchi never shows up in a game, or never has any interactions with your character, I'd say a Lunar will often look at the River Province and add a little sign saying &quot;this space reserved for new goatfolk parking lot in the next ten years&quot;. That's the impression I get from some of the in and out-of-character discussion of the Black Lion.<br /> <br /> Maybe also defines some of the spaces they know they can move readily in. When you're frequently hunted by the Realm, and you now the Realm can't often approach the sphere of Ma-Ha-Suchi or Raksi or the Caul, those places are going to look very attractive as hubs to issue forth from and fall back to.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of this amusing image I once read of 17th-18th century European armies as being like a parrot shifting their legs along the bars of a cage, where the bars are the innovative cannon-proof fortresses that were the strategic lynchpin of the time, and the cage is traditionally disputed territory.<br /> <br /> That and how they're still a major force and figures in the rhetoric of the Silver Pact. It's a matter of how, when there's a lot of talk of reclaiming their stolen entitlement to the Realm, it helps to have some circulation of the influence of the people who saw it first hand. Multi-generational revolutionary movements often place a lot of stock in the people who were part of the first wave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:54:31-07:00","id":287779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287721#post287721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, your example (Good Guy Realm) is an example of simplicity, not complexity, as it attempted to remove ambiguity of PCs or the Realm's imperial state issues. And the parts about where you often detride others for not liking fun for liking complexity, seem to indicate that implictily if not explicitly you find authors should prioritize fun over complexity, whih often to the detriment of nuance in depictions of characters. Your praise of 2e Raksi and your depictions of her in game show this. She is not complex. And you have not seemed to show interest in making her more complex, as that threatens her playability.<br /> <br /> So while you claim your arguments show they can be compatable, the structures of your concerns and examples indicate more often a slide to them being opposed. Which is then why folks respond and criticize your points, as you have not actually argued well that you aren't presenting what many see as a false dichotomy.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not detriding anyone for liking complexity, I'm deriding people for responding before actually reading my posts. I am not deriding the idea that a more complex Raksi would be <i>bad </i>I'm saying her 2e writeup wasn't a &quot;waste of wordcount&quot; because it was <i>still useful</i> for an antagonist. Furthermore, &quot;Good Guy Realm&quot; is an attepmet at complexity and the arguments against me up till this point haven't even <i>denied that</i> so much as insisted that this is a good thing. Bro, do you even read things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:06:49-07:00","id":287787,"title":"","content":"You guys aren't thinking about things that will make Creation a cool place to run a campaign; your thinking about things that will be cool to <i>read about</i> in a setting book.<br /> <br /> The way all of you seem to want the Exalted setting to be handled, barring egregious metagaming, would turn nearly <i>every single Solar game </i>it into this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/AZComics/comic371.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Don't you want a little more variety than that? Don't you think that's unnecessarily limiting? Or are you all just planning on metagaming so your Solar PCs behave like they know all of Creations secret, important complexities? You guys keep talking about how this stuff is useful, how the mark of a <i>true</i> Solar will be how he plans around it but in all likelihood you will <i>never</i> know about any of this in-character and that itself <i>perfectly illustrates my point </i>about prioritizing complexity over playability.<br /> <br /> And before <i>someone</i> brings it up; having a Lore rating of 5 doesn't entitle you to know the secret lives of the setting's important NPCs!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-20-2014, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:08:03-07:00","id":287789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287779#post287779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Good Guy Realm&quot; is an attepmet at complexity</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but going straight to it does feel like a bit of a slipper slope fallacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying her 2e writeup wasn't a &quot;waste of wordcount&quot; because it was <i>still useful</i> for an antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, I feel that an antagonist of that level of sophistication really doesn't need much said about them, unless one has players who need to be really, <i>really</i> motivated to kill simple bad guys by an extensive list of their atrocities. There are Guild villains who manage to be more interesting in their villainy, and still pretty abhorren, without needing half the words Raksi got.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T10:22:33-07:00","id":287796,"title":"","content":"Everything about Malahanka is basically part of Raksi's write-up. Because <i>what else</i> are you going to do there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T15:41:42-07:00","id":288031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys aren't thinking about things that will make Creation a cool place to run a campaign; your thinking about things that will be cool to read about in a setting book.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I should thank my one and indivisible God that you're here to tell me what I do and don't find fun, eh? Here I was thinking that a setting that has some moral and social complexity and isn't completely culturally tone deaf was something that some experiences, fun or otherwise, could be had in, but now I see the light. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are you all just planning on metagaming so your Solar PCs behave like they know all of Creations secret, important complexities?</div> </div> </div> </div> Do... do you think that a bit of developed or intuitive knowledge of the idea that powerful people might be useful and governments cause problems when they collapse and general consideration for the consequences of ones actions is some kind of magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T17:13:10-07:00","id":288080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288031#post288031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, I should thank my one and indivisible God that you're here to tell me what I do and don't find fun, eh? Here I was thinking that a setting that has some moral and social complexity and isn't completely culturally tone deaf was something that some experiences, fun or otherwise, could be had in, but now I see the light. Do... do you think that a bit of developed or intuitive knowledge of the idea that powerful people might be useful and governments cause problems when they collapse and general consideration for the consequences of ones actions is some kind of magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>For example:<br /> <br /> If a more <i>complex, nuanced</i> 3e Raksi's behavior is just an act then it's metagaming for your character to act like he <i>knows</i> it's just an act because <i>very few PCs </i>will ever find that out. You of <i>course </i>plan for the <i>foreseeable</i> consequences of your actions but you can't <i>predict</i> the secret lives of important powerful NPCs because that's out of character knowledge.<br /> <br /> In this case a more complex Raksi is useless (or even detrimental) for 9/10 Solar campaigns. It does make the setting books more entertaining for people to <i>read</i> but the purpose of an NPC writeup shouldn't be how cool it is to <i>read about</i>, it should be <i>helpful</i> for running a game. This universe exists for <i>running games; </i>its a campaign setting! That's what campaign settings are for!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-20-2014, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T17:14:31-07:00","id":288081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288031#post288031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do... do you think that a bit of developed or intuitive knowledge of the idea that powerful people might be useful and governments cause problems when they collapse and general consideration for the consequences of ones actions is some kind of magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it does appear to be some kind of magic given how many revolutionaries never seem to learn those lessons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T18:47:20-07:00","id":288128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287787#post287787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys aren't thinking about things that will make Creation a cool place to run a campaign; your thinking about things that will be cool to <i>read about</i> in a setting book.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I get at where you present your case in a framework that's a false dichotomy. You seem to think that making Creation interesting and complex is somehow something I have to put at odds with fun. It isn't. While you have caveated that they aren't dichotomous, you seem to still argue that trying to create complexity at all leads to lack of playability. So what's the solution? Make things simple black and white and simple? Why is that preferrable? How is that better for everyone? Why can't I have complexity in presentation and it still be a fun game in dealing with the results of pushing the complexity a bit?<br /> <br /> When I play, I like it when I do something like kill a big bad, it does something beside sme getting loot, as big bads isolated in the wilderness might as well not be there as far as the setting as a whole is concerned. If killing someone even like Raksi has no consequences, why have a character like Raksi in this setting? Is the role of powerful antagonists as yous ee it to be pi\u00f1atas for stuff and glory? If killing her only just makes things suck less for the world, why hasn't she been killed by other people who have more interests in the world than having her fuck it up? If she wasnt' important enough to kill before, why does your role in killing her matter now?<br /> <br /> And in all of that, I like to run Exalted, and I like nuance presented when I run it. I don't need wordcount wasted on what amounts to a loser in the middle of nowhere who when killed no one will care if missed. If I get an antagonist written-up and if she has a big &quot;kill me&quot; signal going, I kind of want it to be shown what the consequences of killing her might be besides being able to get goodies and pat yoursel fon the back of a job well done. I'd rather have someone like the Lady, Zhirek, Lord Genome, or Zhaheer than what amounts to a Power Rangers villain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287787#post287787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way all of you seem to want the Exalted setting to be handled, barring egregious metagaming, would turn nearly <i>every single Solar game </i>it into this:<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice strawman.<br /> <br /> The issue you have is accusing nuance and wanting that as metagaming. Folks read the books, sure. But the alternative is more or less 2D cutouts in a setting and that's moot. That you doing stuff will lead to maybe bad stuff happening is fine for a lot of games. THat's how the World of Darkness franchises work, as well as Shadowrun, and even D&amp;D settings like Dark Sun. What matters isn't folks wandeirng into something stupid. It's them doing things that lead to interesting stories and plots. Actions have consequences is a mantra of Exalted since Day One. This is the buy-in that a lot of folks go into the game having. And accusing it as basically players metagamingly acknowledging that they're blithering into fanciful suicide is both insulting to the expected intelligence of the audience, and I think accusing those who like to run or play nuanced games of basically &quot;Doing it wrong because I don't like it.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287787#post287787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you want a little more variety than that? Don't you think that's unnecessarily limiting? Or are you all just planning on metagaming so your Solar PCs behave like they know all of Creations secret, important complexities? ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a jump of logic. The issue you seem to think is that if the books write things more complexly, and players know the world has more complexity, then there's....metagaming with that complexity in mind? I am not sure what your point is on this. I can still build a character who runs around like a naive shounen hero and just know as a player that this might burn me. That's fine enough. I don't have to play as if the compelxities are there. It's just better if that gives me 1) Interesting allies to deal with and antagonists for the ST to toss at me and 2) Makes it so that I know my ST has more options to work with or interesitng plots ot work with than what would otherwise amount to reskinned D&amp;D. Which well, I have D&amp;D to do that if I need to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287787#post287787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... You guys keep talking about how this stuff is useful, how the mark of a <i>true</i> Solar will be how he plans around it but in all likelihood you will <i>never</i> know about any of this in-character and that itself <i>perfectly illustrates my point </i>about prioritizing complexity over playability.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you authors shouldn't even bother? Or is the issue that you seem to be thinking people are not as deep as they claim to be? You seem ot have thi smindset that folks who want depth don't want fun. Or that if we want depth, we'll let that influence our games and we'll never knwo it in-character, so why bother. This is somewhat fatalistic in one sense, and I feel again, characterizes a style of game you don't like as not fun because it's not your style. Tough shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287787#post287787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And before <i>someone</i> brings it up; having a Lore rating of 5 doesn't entitle you to know the secret lives of the setting's important NPCs!</div> </div> </div> </div>No one said it did. And no one arguing of nuance is arguing that their character should be privvy to this knowledge. I could very well make a character who wants to kill Raksi because of the very reasons you argued earlier in the thread. And I don't have any qualms letting that happen. That her write-up more or less makes this the only reason you interact with her, and you are in effect rewarded with a consequenceless victory for doing so is the problem that even brought this up. It means her write-up was shitty since it didn't really present here as anything more than some useless psychotic hermit who needed to be euthanized (something easily said in much less wordcount than she got) and it also means that she wasn't worth even that as in the grand scheme of things she only served as an excuse for heroes patting themselves on the back for a monster well-slain. You can get the same out of a mindless behemoth. And that only needs a couple pages to write-about rather than a treasure city, dozens of tribes, and a supposed warmachine that doesn't do much but dither about.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T18:50:22-07:00","id":288129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288080#post288080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a more <i>complex, nuanced</i> 3e Raksi's behavior is just an act then it's metagaming for your character to act like he <i>knows</i> it's just an act because <i>very few PCs </i>will ever find that out. You of <i>course </i>plan for the <i>foreseeable</i> consequences of your actions but you can't <i>predict</i> the secret lives of important powerful NPCs because that's out of character knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Malahanka is extremely far East with Farhold as the only canonical place within striking distance, the idea that her depravities are accurately documented that a scholar from the Scavenger Lands can just know that Raksi eats babies and that it's not some bullshit Immaculate account.<br /> <br /> It gives me amusing mental images that she's somehow got a published autobiography entitled &quot;Unrepentant Baby Eater, My Story&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-20-2014, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T18:56:35-07:00","id":288132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288080#post288080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example:<br /> <br /> If a more <i>complex, nuanced</i> 3e Raksi's behavior is just an act then it's metagaming for your character to act like he <i>knows</i> it's just an act because <i>very few PCs </i>will ever find that out. You of <i>course </i>plan for the <i>foreseeable</i> consequences of your actions but you can't <i>predict</i> the secret lives of important powerful NPCs because that's out of character knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Continuing on my post.<br /> <br /> A more nuanced Raksi write-up shows options to interact with her besides just killing her. It describes what she does in an area overtly so that yes, you plan to deal with it effectively. This doens't give cart blanch to act as if you know her write-up. It simply means that 1) Getting to her is harder as she might have more between you and her than a bunch of physical threats, 2) Her having Mahalanka up to now and suddenly not might have consequences, and 3) Her warmachine and how she interacts with it might have something important to think on, but most of the time won't matter for PC reasons if STs incentivze it enough to still just off her.<br /> <br /> The issue, again, seems to me to be that you don't give a shit about something other than a nugget for single one-off encounters. NPCs like Raksi aren't just boss fights, they're setting pieces (who can be used as a boss fight if need be). She exists as much in a way to describe the setting as a write-up of a city, or the structure fo the Guild. They're meant to be regional powers that might be allies, long-term antagonists, or sources of lore. The worry you have on metagaming too hard to me reads like complaining about how if they talk about a city too much folks will metagame how best to navigate it. This is an issue of player knoweldge in general and it is not the game's job to police that or itself with tha tin mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288080#post288080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case a more complex Raksi is useless (or even detrimental) for 9/10 Solar campaigns. It does make the setting books more entertaining for people to <i>read</i> but the purpose of an NPC writeup shouldn't be how cool it is to <i>read about</i>, it should be <i>helpful</i> for running a game. This universe exists for <i>running games; </i>its a campaign setting! That's what campaign settings are for!</div> </div> </div> </div>A psychotic hermit in a corner of Creation no one gives a shit about half the time and who has a magic book no one can use for most of history is not very helpful compared to someone who (as presented in 1e at least) was a local power player, and possible long term plot element. A more nuanced Raksi is useful in more games in dint in having more ways to interact with games, either as someone alive to be a problem or someone of more consequences if dead. Her 2e write-up by contrast is in essence no better than a D&amp;D or Pathfinder game with an evil NPC immortal running ar uined city for thousands of years and not hurting anyone. SUre it's nasty, but in the end she's kind of useless and no better than a rogue automota or behemoth save for flavor text.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T19:58:18-07:00","id":288173,"title":"","content":"<br /> I see you're still quite confused on &quot;I don't think Exalted should be complex&quot; vs. &quot;I think fun and playability should be <i>prioritized </i>(in a <i>game)</i> over complexity&quot; I don't know what I can do about this behavior on your part besides repeat myself.<br /> <br /> Oh, this is actually helpful to talk about, though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288128#post288128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in all of that, I like to run Exalted, and I like nuance presented when I run it. I don't need wordcount wasted on what amounts to a loser in the middle of nowhere who when killed no one will care if missed. If I get an antagonist written-up and if she has a big &quot;kill me&quot; signal going, I kind of want it to be shown what the consequences of killing her might be besides being able to get goodies and pat yoursel fon the back of a job well done. I'd rather have someone like the Lady, Zhirek, Lord Genome, or Zhaheer than what amounts to a Power Rangers villain.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e Raksi wasn\u2019t like this at all because she <i>still</i> had power and influence in the Silver Pact and the consequences of killing her were drawing <i>huge</i> attention to your Circle from members of that organization who weren\u2019t fans of upstart Solars (especially Solars who showed a willingness to off Lunar Elders). This is complexity, but thankfully it isn\u2019t complexity that gets in the way of playability or fun by unduly punishing PCs for killing a <i>baby-eating, civilization-destroying, masochistic, Wyld-tainted pseudo-chimera. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288128#post288128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a jump of logic. The issue you seem to think is that if the books write things more complexly, and players know the world has more complexity, then there's....metagaming with that complexity in mind? I am not sure what your point is on this. I can still build a character who runs around like a naive shounen hero and just know as a player that this might burn me. That's fine enough. I don't have to play as if the compelxities are there. It's just better if that gives me 1) Interesting allies to deal with and antagonists for the ST to toss at me and 2) Makes it so that I know my ST has more options to work with or interesitng plots ot work with than what would otherwise amount to reskinned D&amp;D. Which well, I have D&amp;D to do that if I need to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless your actual <i>goal </i>when you run Exalted is, like, masochism these models aren\u2019t practical for actual (non-Sidreal) campaigns because the default assumption for Solar campaigns is you <i>are</i> a Clueless Shonen Hero and the setting is <i>fucking unplayable </i>if it is <i>designed </i>to make Clueless Shonen Heroes feel miserable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T20:20:51-07:00","id":288180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288173#post288173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see you're still quite confused on &quot;I don't think Exalted should be complex&quot; vs. &quot;I think fun and playability should be <i>prioritized </i>(in a <i>game)</i> over complexity&quot; I don't know what I can do about this behavior on your part besides repeat myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know full well what you mean. I just think that it's a set of behaviro very reminescent of specific sorts of games that aren't Exalted. I think the fact that you claim this is an RPG thing in general when listing Shadowrun and World of Darkness, both games where you are expected to play chacters prone to very bad decisisons, and not expect that out of Exalted, is a tad bizrre to me. And I keep bringing up the point since desptie your claims otherwise, your arguments and tone to me end up you basically saying one thing and arguing the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288173#post288173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> 2e Raksi wasn\u2019t like this at all because she <i>still</i> had power and influence in the Silver Pact and the consequences of killing her were drawing <i>huge</i> attention to your Circle from members of that organization who weren\u2019t fans of upstart Solars (especially Solars who showed a willingness to off Lunar Elders). This is complexity, but thankfully it isn\u2019t complexity that gets in the way of playability or fun by unduly punishing PCs for killing a <i>baby-eating, civilization-destroying, masochistic, Wyld-tainted pseudo-chimera. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with this is a fewfold. First, in her 2e writeup her crowning acheivements appear to be helping develop tattoos and being a psychopath locking away Mahalanka. Whatever influence hse had on the Silver Pact is nto talked about and the Silver Pact in 2e was itself designed fairly poorly to not have much worth to being influential in. She, like Leviathan to some extent, more or less brooded in the middle of nowhere not doing anything it appears of note. And unlike Leviathan, she didn't even have the sanity to do a lot anyhow.<br /> <br /> Also, while her baby-eating and Wyld-mutatning were bad, again, they're kind of emphasized on her character to the point that killing her is a pat ont eh back. Nothing happens if you kill her save her allies getting upset (this is good seeing consequences of yoru actions) and you get as a reward a big fucking city with magic stuff and a person killed no one will miss. The issue with her being a psychopath is that she wasn't really useful for anything but an aformentioend pi\u00f1ata for toys. <br /> <br /> You seem to also as a note be conflating competence (which her 2e write-up sorely lacked) with complexity. As Lioness pointed out, sure she was eating babies and such, but was in the middle of nowhere and more or less not doing anything else anyone gave a shit about save being crazy. She's not even that civlization-destroying, as nothing in her 2e write-up seemed to indicate anything but a shallow attempt of insanity and obsession over the Book of Three Circles. Killing her won't stop the Thousand Fangs Army or suddenly make her apeman horde less an apeman horde. And that the only real consequence is that you got to feel good putting down a crazy mosnter (which again, you can do with killing a behemoth) and pissing some elders off (which you can do with any elder) isn't complexity. It just makes her pretty much a cut-out villain who doens't need more than af ew paragraphs, as the end reuslt is, &quot;Crazy hermit witch cannibal be crazy, and her dying might upset some people.&quot;<br /> <br /> I will also note that her 2e presentation is a simplification. As in 1e she was a cannibal monster who just happened to not give a shit what you thought of her being a cannibal monster and also cmpetent. 2e kind of just went and emphasized the cannibal monster part at expense of her ability to be relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288173#post288173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your actual <i>goal </i>when you run Exalted is, like, masochism these models aren\u2019t practical for actual (non-Sidreal) campaigns because the default assumption for Solar campaigns is you <i>are</i> a Clueless Shonen Hero and the setting is <i>fucking unplayable </i>if it is <i>designed </i>to make Clueless Shonen Heroes feel miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making life complicated for your clueless shonen heroes isn't making it miserable for them. Which again, seems to be your jumping into the false dichotmy of nuance for actions and fun. <br /> <br /> A lot of your posts seem to be, despite your arguments of drawing on other games, very founded on D&amp;D principles, as a note. The game ins't menat to be a set of discreent encounters where you break shit and get loot and then no conseuqences for that bleed into different stories. Killing the boss at hte end shouldn't be the end of the arc, get xp, mvoe on. Raksi dies, things happen because a big facet of the setting changed. Abandoned cities in the middle of fucking nowhere with immortal sorceres dithering about waiting for adventers to kill them for the good of the world or whatever is something that fits say, Pathfinder (I played in an official module a few months ago that was jus this actually). In Exalted, if the important city is abandoned because of a sorcerer-queen, it's probably for a good fucking reason. And if you kill her, there are going to be things besides &quot;Her long-term but far away ambiguous friends are mad&quot; are expected conseuqneces, as suddenly the person in charge of the big magic occult city is no longer there to dominate it.<br /> <br /> The issue seems to be you have a very specific view of what equates fun and how one runs a game that is fun. The problem you're finding is others don't agree with you on this, and characterizing how we prefer games to be in negative or ssadistic a light seems if anything confirming my view that you have a very limitted way in which enjoyable RPGs are menat to be played.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T21:16:28-07:00","id":288228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288129#post288129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malahanka is extremely far East with Farhold as the only canonical place within striking distance, the idea that her depravities are accurately documented that a scholar from the Scavenger Lands can just know that Raksi eats babies and that it's not some bullshit Immaculate account.<br /> <br /> It gives me amusing mental images that she's somehow got a published autobiography entitled &quot;Unrepentant Baby Eater, My Story&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the sidebar, &quot;My secret recipe for infant vindaloo&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T21:52:56-07:00","id":288244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288173#post288173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless your actual <i>goal </i>when you run Exalted is, like, masochism these models aren\u2019t practical for actual (non-Sidreal) campaigns because the default assumption for Solar campaigns is you <i>are</i> a Clueless Shonen Hero and the setting is <i>fucking unplayable </i>if it is <i>designed </i>to make Clueless Shonen Heroes feel miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, DBs are intended to be a PLAYER SPLAT.<br /> <br /> *DEEP BREATH*<br /> <br /> Okay, I think you are just coming at this from a completely different angle. What you perceive as being the default way to play Exalted is not what the other people in this topic perceive as the default, and those things you perceive as being in the way of fun are precisely the things people here find fun. You're not going to suddenly convert someone to your side and because of the difference in perception, you seem to have difficulty in describing your position without insulting the position of others in the conversation. I'd suggest going back and reading carefully over the topic and your part in it and decide how and if you want to continue this.<br /> <br /> I encourage everyone else in the topic to tread carefully as well, I don't think Ranger_Lord really intends to come off quite as he does and I encourage others who continue conversing with him to bare in mind he seems to have a radically different perception of what Exalted is and should be, not just what it is in his own game.<br /> <br /> That's just my perception of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T03:00:22-07:00","id":288436,"title":"","content":"When I imagine figures like Raksi, I tend towards the idea of certain fairy tale monsters and villains, where the idea that they have a tendency to eat children is present as an off-putting and uncanny detail, but may not be the focus of the tale (unless the protagonist happens to be or have a child), nor completely overwhelm the character or any interactions with or responses to them. This includes narratives where your encounter ends with you being relieved to have gotten away intact, while being... not exactly unconcerned, but not really wanting to know how the character will conduct themselves thereafter.<br /> <br /> It's like, I quite like the Baba Yaga from Hellboy, and don't think that everything to do with her has to focus on outrage at the fact that she's eaten children.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that, depending on what culture in Creation you come from, your sense of the sanctity of human life and the preciousness of children, especially the youngest infants, may sometimes lack an especially visceral sense of moral outrage at certain forms of murder, at least if it's something abstract that you're not directly exposed to. Certain prior time periods had people a bit less attached to babies who were very likely to just up and die anyway, not counting occasions where they're deliberately left to exposure because there are too many mouths to feed or have some undesirable disfiguration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T03:03:50-07:00","id":288437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288173#post288173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Unless your actual <i>goal </i>when you run Exalted is, like, masochism these models aren\u2019t practical for actual (non-Sidreal) campaigns because the default assumption for Solar campaigns is you <i>are</i> a Clueless Shonen Hero and the setting is <i>fucking unplayable </i>if it is <i>designed </i>to make Clueless Shonen Heroes feel miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your default model is strange to me, and deserves to be challenged.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T04:04:45-07:00","id":288448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=286854#post286854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like King Louie.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://38.media.tumblr.com/db591ea8edc8da16e84fbce0ababc716/tumblr_n2xtcgJPEr1tqs1heo1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img3.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20140717131046/kingdom-hearts-unlimited/images/0/0f/Queen_La.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T05:37:17-07:00","id":288466,"title":"","content":"I've also got this image that, as a Changing Moon Caste, a figure like Ma-Ha-Suchi should be a lot like Bill Cutting from Gangs of New York in terms of how he looks to somebody who comes wanting to kill him for his crimes, in terms of how despite how he's a dreadful person who has wronged you specifically, he's also extremely charismatic and knows how to win folks over with a combination of his own force of personality and the contacts and rewards he can provide. He might even have a certain tragic, Romantic air to him that elicits sympathy despite one's better judgement (although I can imagine a rather different emotional context to him ruminating on how civilization is crumbling). This is the kind of thing that can make it hard not to be conflicted about following through even if he's still amassing an army trained to do things like use rape as a weapon (in a manner a bit more realistic than the Rutting Pens).<br /> <br /> Likewise with Raksi, although I imagine her way of tying up and weighing down people who come to her with vengeance and justice in their hearts is a bit more intellectual or instructional. She's got a lot to teach, and might even be a bit forceful in providing it, at least at first so you can get enough of a taste to want to keep going with it. That can lead off in a few directions, including where she always tries to have a bit more to reveal so they never think they can afford to kill her yet, or after so long with her they're enamoured or impressed or even just familiar enough with her that killing her doesn't seem to fit anymore, or even just that in the course of things one has had to become so morally compromised that they no longer really think they're in a position to judge her.<br /> <br /> Also with the idea that Raksi isn't stupid, and knows that her conduct will bring some people who'll want to strike at her head on, and has preparations to deal with such folks, maybe preferring to pin them in place while she works her literal and proverbial magic on them (which is probably less smart, or being too smart for one's own good).<br /> <br /> Or it can just be that more righteous characters still have Investigation and Socialize as Abilities, and might analyze situations to try and discern the motivations and characteristics behind certain fearsome acts.<br /> <br /> And really, none of this actually excludes taking Raksi down in a straightforward hero narrative, just so long as one is willing to acknowledge that such things don't actually require utterly unambiguous and irreddemable villains. I would personally run through such scenarios against people a lot less terrible than Raksi or Ma-Ha-Suchi without any sense of conflict. Somketimes it'll even be with characters who are just bestest buddies with those terrifying ancient Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T07:45:12-07:00","id":288529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=287671#post287671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The White Rose coming back doens't mean shit if she can't acutally run things when she gets the job done.</div> </div> </div> </div>10/10 enjoyment of a Chronicles of the Black Company reference (whether or not that was your intent).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T08:30:16-07:00","id":288555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288529#post288529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10/10 enjoyment of a Chronicles of the Black Company reference (whether or not that was your intent).</div> </div> </div> </div>It indeed was.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T09:10:29-07:00","id":288608,"title":"","content":"I think that if there's anything we can take away from this, it's that Compass: East was a bad book on so many different levels. Raksi's writeup there is pretty much peak 2E, and there's really not a single way in which it doesn't piss me off. Making her a perpetual teenager with a +3 specialty in fuckability was just the cherry on the shit sundae, and I can only hope that whomever made <i>that </i>call isn't writing for 3E.<br /> <br /> Edit: For what it's worth, Compass: North was wonderful, Gethamane excepted, and Compass: South's handling of An-Teng set my high-water mark for the edition as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T19:15:26-07:00","id":289166,"title":"","content":"Playability doesn't in any sense require that killing Raksi will make the world a better place, or be without calamitous downsides. If those things aren't <i>themselves</i> interesting fodder for a game, then it might, but &quot;everything goes to hell in the Far East&quot; sounds like a pretty great follow-up to &quot;your circle treks to Mahalanka and ganks Raksi&quot;.<br /> <br /> Is there actually a playability issue here, or is it just that the game isn't specifically patting you on the back for improving society by killing the baby-eating ancient monster? Because I can't see that impacting playability much. Meanwhile, the game does actually need an answer to &quot;why hasn't anyone else done this thing yet, given that there are groups more powerful than you out there&quot;, and &quot;because it's pragmatically unwise&quot; seems like a pretty good one.<br /> <br /> One experience I keep coming back to in discussions like this, because it exemplifies the matter for me: at one point in a Solar game we had a huge pile of XP, a strong power base, and a lot of experience under our belt, and we had about a year to kill, so my guy was just like &quot;hey, let's go find Bluehaven and kill all the Lintha,&quot; and the rest of the party was all &quot;yeah sure&quot;. So we roused up an army and sailed it to Bluehaven and beat up Dukantha and had a pitched battle against the Lintha and their demons and then systematically put them all to the sword, except for a handful allowed to leave to spread our legend to their pawns and relatives scattered throughout the world. Was that <i>the right thing to do?</i> Would the destabilization it created cause more damage than the benefits? Was specifically going out of our way to incite the scattered remnants of the Lintha to wage war on us forever a prudent decision? The game ended soon after, so we'll never know, but seriously, <i>who even cares.</i> It made a good story, and the fallout would have also made a good story if it was going to make a story at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 10-21-2014, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T19:43:12-07:00","id":289171,"title":"","content":"I think that there's a difference between &quot;interesting stuff happens, whatever you do&quot; (which is how I generally read the way things are set up) and &quot;everything you do results in the world becoming shit, because it's doomed to be shit, and because you, the person playing this game, are shit for thinking otherwise&quot;, which is I think what some people are afraid of.<br /> <br /> In general I think the game is not designed to have an easy obvious ending, so there's few characters that are just &quot;killing this person is an obvious choice and will solve everything in their region.&quot; It's also somewhat designed with the premise that killing is (comparatively) easy but often has drawbacks. None of these things mean that killing Raksi is necessarily going to be clearly the <i>wrong</i> choice (it depends on how she's played in your game, and the situation you find yourself in), but it does mean that the game isn't designed to make it easy to say &quot;all right, we've killed Raksi, now everything is fixed forever here and the story is over.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T19:57:06-07:00","id":290224,"title":"","content":"So, in other words, &quot;you're probably going to want to gank Raksi, because it's probably a necessary but not sufficient condition to resolve the problems in her region&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4100-powerofvoid","name":"powerofvoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4100_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T20:37:28-07:00","id":290264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>powerofvoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290224#post290224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in other words, &quot;you're probably going to want to gank Raksi, because it's probably a necessary but not sufficient condition to resolve the problems in her region&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason it's necessary. If the players figure out another way the ST should allow them to try it, and it probably shouldn't be completely doomed to failure from the start as a default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T21:12:35-07:00","id":290279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>powerofvoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290224#post290224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in other words, &quot;you're probably going to want to gank Raksi, because it's probably a necessary but not sufficient condition to resolve the problems in her region&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily <i>necessary</i>, no. It might be necessary or it might not. Your Solar might wonder beforehand if there is another way. You might wonder afterwards if you made the right choice. The game probably isn't going to hand you an easy answer to that -- it makes for a better story to leave it uncertain.<br /> <br /> Conversely, it's not going to say &quot;killing Raksi is <i>very definitely</i> wrong and will inevitably screw everything up forever&quot;, for similar reasons. This also means that the problems with Raksi likely won't come down to one issue of wyld mutations or derangements -- putting aside the problem people mentioned above about how this is a game where playing the Ultimate Doctor or Ultimate Sorcerer who can cure even those things is an intended playstyle, I think that it is somewhat boring to make the problems caused by a problem come from their Evil Gene or Evil Sickness or whatever, which can be punched out of their body or surgically removed and then everything will be all right.<br /> <br /> Raksi doesn't eat people and rule a city of ape-men cannibals because she is twisted by the Wyld or because she's an innocent who was corrupted by some obvious Evil Mutation. She does it because she believes that that is her natural right and because mortal humans are literally no more than animals to her. This is what she actually believes, something expressed in everything she has said and done for the past fifteen hundred years; it's entirely possible that she has never believed otherwise. &quot;Redeeming&quot; her is not a simple matter of giving one speech or hitting her with the magic Cure Evil charm. The cannibal-queen of Spermin is partially a guise she puts on, sure, but the things she <i>does</i> in that role are things she totally feels she's entitled to do as a Lunar Exalt.<br /> <br /> The other alternative (and the much easier one) is to say &quot;well, the number of people she eats is an acceptable cost for the number she saves by acting as one of Creation's defenders.&quot; But I don't think that that should be an easy call to make, either. There's a bigger cost to having her around than just the people she eats directly. She's a symbol of what Lunars (and Anathema) <i>are</i>, to most people. If you cut a deal with her, people will see you the same way. If she survives into whatever new world your characters are fighting for, she's going to be a part of shaping that world, which includes teaching a new generation of Exalted that, hey, it's all right to eat a few people now and then, you know?<br /> <br /> <br /> Naturally, this is all stuff that will vary from game to game -- I suspect that Raksi's write-up will be designed so using her as a straightforward antagonist is one option but not the only option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-11-2015, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T21:18:17-07:00","id":290282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>powerofvoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290224#post290224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in other words, &quot;you're probably going to want to gank Raksi, because it's probably a necessary but not sufficient condition to resolve the problems in her region&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>At <i>some</i> point, if your goal is to turn the whole East into a region without problems, you are going to need to deal with Raksi, because Raksi is absolutely a problem. It's not hard to imagine that the right time to do that is well outside the scope of a normal campaign, though, or that the best way to do it is not to go there personally and stab her to death. Certainly, it's pretty easy to justify <i>not</i> trying to kill Raksi in a game where your goal is to turn the East into a glorious utopia, even if theoretically you would want her dead somewhere down the road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 10-26-2014, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T01:48:10-07:00","id":290374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290282#post290282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At <i>some</i> point, if your goal is to turn the whole East into a region without problems, you are going to need to deal with Raksi, because Raksi is absolutely a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if she's just next door. Indeed, I'd say there are more likely to be Exalts who come into some kind of conflict with Raksi because she's right over there than because they've got an Eastern Liberation Project going on.<br /> <br /> Really, even the idea of wanting to kill Raksi, for whatever reason, doesn't have to be something characters are seriously impeded from doing by demands that they consider the consequences beforehand (even if they might deal with them afterwards). That's distinct from the image of her being a straw doll with a scary face drawn on that everybody can feel righteous about cutting down, <i>even if one plays a character who kills Raksi for that reason</i>.<br /> <br /> In any case, the style and system still has more options to bring somebody around than killing them. Not even necessarily making Raksi nice, possibly just bringing her to heel a bit.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T11:19:48-07:00","id":290678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288448#post288448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://img3.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20140717131046/kingdom-hearts-unlimited/images/0/0f/Queen_La.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Checking the dates,<i> Exalted the Lunars</i> was released in 2002, whereas the Tarzan cartoon aired in 2001.<br /> <br /> But Raksi seems to take just as much inspiration from King Louie, afterall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T11:30:53-07:00","id":290686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290678#post290678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Checking the dates,<i> Exalted the Lunars</i> was released in 2002, whereas the Tarzan cartoon aired in 2001.<br /> <br /> But Raksi seems to take just as much inspiration from King Louie, afterall.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cartoon aired in 2001, but the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_%28Tarzan%29\" target=\"_blank\">book</a> was published in 1913.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I don't think Raksi much resembles La or Louie at this juncture. 2E made her more crazy and psychotic than either of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T11:56:04-07:00","id":290700,"title":"","content":"I've honestly never seen how Raksi is supposed to have drawn inspiration from King Louie.<br /> Though that might be because the only people I've seen make any kind of comparison between them were mocking Raksi with the comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T12:02:01-07:00","id":290703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290700#post290700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've honestly never seen how Raksi is supposed to have drawn inspiration from King Louie.<br /> Though that might be because the only people I've seen make any kind of comparison between them were mocking Raksi with the comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I recall first seeing the comparison around the time Reminiscent Oasis did her version of Raksi for the TAW Lunars. Maybe it came up sooner? In any case, I definitely don't buy King Louie as an actual inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T12:03:22-07:00","id":290705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290700#post290700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've honestly never seen how Raksi is supposed to have drawn inspiration from King Louie.<br /> Though that might be because the only people I've seen make any kind of comparison between them were mocking Raksi with the comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>'She wants to learn Solar Sorcery' -&gt; 'She wants to be an awesome Solar instead of a sucky Lunar but is doomed to failure' -&gt;<i> 'I wanna be like you, an ape like me, can learn to be human tooo~'</i><br /> <br /> Let's just hope that's a wild exaggeration and never actually crossed the mind of a writer, otherwise someone is in need of a good slapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T13:10:31-07:00","id":290739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290705#post290705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'She wants to learn Solar Sorcery' -&gt; 'She wants to be an awesome Solar instead of a sucky Lunar but is doomed to failure' -&gt;<i> 'I wanna be like you, an ape like me, can learn to be human tooo~'</i><br /> <br /> Let's just hope that's a wild exaggeration and never actually crossed the mind of a writer, otherwise someone is in need of a good slapping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now that you've gone and <i>posted it</i> on the <i>official forums</i>...<br /> <br /> Of <i>course</i> it's going to cross the mind of a writer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4100-powerofvoid","name":"powerofvoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4100_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T13:15:05-07:00","id":290742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290700#post290700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've honestly never seen how Raksi is supposed to have drawn inspiration from King Louie.<br /> Though that might be because the only people I've seen make any kind of comparison between them were mocking Raksi with the comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) You don't need to be inspired by King Louie to <i>be</i> King Louie.<br /> 2) Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T13:21:11-07:00","id":290744,"title":"","content":"It just feels very Second Edition to me.<br /> Exalted: the Lunars spent a lot of time beating its chest and acting like the Solars were unnecessary for me to think someone did that intentionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 10-23-2014, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:47:51-07:00","id":290825,"title":"","content":"Queen La appears associated with Leopards, and seems to want Tarzan rather than a power beyond her understanding. King Louie and his followers are apes, and he wants power beyond his understanding. Raki wants power beyond understanding, has never been associated with a Solar mate, and her totem and beast men are apes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:58:07-07:00","id":290834,"title":"","content":"The ultimate inspiration for Raksi is probably <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/She:_A_History_of_Adventure\" target=\"_blank\">She</a>, which is the ur-source of the magical immortal jungle queen narrative (and probably had a lot of influence, if indirectly, on Lunars in general.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-23-2014, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T06:10:25-07:00","id":291224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=290834#post290834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ultimate inspiration for Raksi is probably <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/She:_A_History_of_Adventure\" target=\"_blank\">She</a>, which is the ur-source of the magical immortal jungle queen narrative (and probably had a lot of influence, if indirectly, on Lunars in general.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Stephen Lea Sheppard has said as much elsewhere, which is why I said I'd rather see her as Kurtz/Colonel Kurtz from <i>Heart of Darkness/Apocalypse Now</i>, because I most sincerely doubt one could ever salvage something that deeply, hilariously racist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T06:57:02-07:00","id":291307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291224#post291224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stephen Lea Sheppard has said as much elsewhere, which is why I said I'd rather see her as Kurtz/Colonel Kurtz from <i>Heart of Darkness/Apocalypse Now</i>, because I most sincerely doubt one could ever salvage something that deeply, hilariously racist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, folks still read Lovecraft. I think folks are actually pretty good at just kind of setting aside that sort of stuff if the material is old enough to get the Old Timey Racism label. And since She is kind of an archetypical character at this point, there are probably other characters to work on from her that work out just fine.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T07:37:29-07:00","id":291334,"title":"","content":"I was trying to think of examples of cases where people interact with a large and fearsome figure who has probably eaten some of their own kind without it being a moral judgement issue.<br /> <br /> The Great Owl from The Secret of NIMH seems like a fairly good reference for an elder Lunar in general, and possibly Raksi in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T10:01:21-07:00","id":291433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288180#post288180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know full well what you mean. I just think that it's a set of behaviro very reminescent of specific sorts of games that aren't Exalted. I think the fact that you claim this is an RPG thing in general when listing Shadowrun and World of Darkness, both games where you are expected to play chacters prone to very bad decisisons, and not expect that out of Exalted, is a tad bizrre to me. And I keep bringing up the point since desptie your claims otherwise, your arguments and tone to me end up you basically saying one thing and arguing the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> The issue with this is a fewfold. First, in her 2e writeup her crowning acheivements appear to be helping develop tattoos and being a psychopath locking away Mahalanka. Whatever influence hse had on the Silver Pact is nto talked about and the Silver Pact in 2e was itself designed fairly poorly to not have much worth to being influential in. She, like Leviathan to some extent, more or less brooded in the middle of nowhere not doing anything it appears of note. And unlike Leviathan, she didn't even have the sanity to do a lot anyhow.<br /> <br /> Also, while her baby-eating and Wyld-mutatning were bad, again, they're kind of emphasized on her character to the point that killing her is a pat ont eh back. Nothing happens if you kill her save her allies getting upset (this is good seeing consequences of yoru actions) and you get as a reward a big fucking city with magic stuff and a person killed no one will miss. The issue with her being a psychopath is that she wasn't really useful for anything but an aformentioend pi\u00f1ata for toys.<br /> <br /> You seem to also as a note be conflating competence (which her 2e write-up sorely lacked) with complexity. As Lioness pointed out, sure she was eating babies and such, but was in the middle of nowhere and more or less not doing anything else anyone gave a shit about save being crazy. She's not even that civlization-destroying, as nothing in her 2e write-up seemed to indicate anything but a shallow attempt of insanity and obsession over the Book of Three Circles. Killing her won't stop the Thousand Fangs Army or suddenly make her apeman horde less an apeman horde. And that the only real consequence is that you got to feel good putting down a crazy mosnter (which again, you can do with killing a behemoth) and pissing some elders off (which you can do with any elder) isn't complexity. It just makes her pretty much a cut-out villain who doens't need more than af ew paragraphs, as the end reuslt is, &quot;Crazy hermit witch cannibal be crazy, and her dying might upset some people.&quot;<br /> <br /> I will also note that her 2e presentation is a simplification. As in 1e she was a cannibal monster who just happened to not give a shit what you thought of her being a cannibal monster and also cmpetent. 2e kind of just went and emphasized the cannibal monster part at expense of her ability to be relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Making life complicated for your clueless shonen heroes isn't making it miserable for them. Which again, seems to be your jumping into the false dichotmy of nuance for actions and fun.<br /> <br /> A lot of your posts seem to be, despite your arguments of drawing on other games, very founded on D&amp;D principles, as a note. The game ins't menat to be a set of discreent encounters where you break shit and get loot and then no conseuqences for that bleed into different stories. Killing the boss at hte end shouldn't be the end of the arc, get xp, mvoe on. Raksi dies, things happen because a big facet of the setting changed. Abandoned cities in the middle of fucking nowhere with immortal sorceres dithering about waiting for adventers to kill them for the good of the world or whatever is something that fits say, Pathfinder (I played in an official module a few months ago that was jus this actually). In Exalted, if the important city is abandoned because of a sorcerer-queen, it's probably for a good fucking reason. And if you kill her, there are going to be things besides &quot;Her long-term but far away ambiguous friends are mad&quot; are expected conseuqneces, as suddenly the person in charge of the big magic occult city is no longer there to dominate it.<br /> <br /> The issue seems to be you have a very specific view of what equates fun and how one runs a game that is fun. The problem you're finding is others don't agree with you on this, and characterizing how we prefer games to be in negative or ssadistic a light seems if anything confirming my view that you have a very limitted way in which enjoyable RPGs are menat to be played.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geez man, this shit is bananas. You\u2019ve used a lot of really specific and arrogantly dismissive theorycraft here but, it\u2019s ultimately all for nothing because the Silver Pact\u2019s reaction to the PCs killing Raksi is <i>exactly as severe as the ST wants it to be.</i><br /> <br /> Like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=288180#post288180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you kill her, there are going to be things besides &quot;Her long-term but far away ambiguous friends are mad&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The more of your posts I read, the more it looks like you don\u2019t <i>play</i> Exalted as much as read the fluff text for its own sake. This level of vagueness is <i>perfect</i> for STs and players for facilitating any kind of game they want, but if one were to treat the setting books as pleasurable reading for their own sake, then yes, I\u2019d imagine writing like this would be very frustrating.<br /> <br /> I think Exalted can stand to have a few (a few!) encounters that are traditional dungeon crawls. The setting is not <i>made worse</i> by having more variety from session to session and different kinds of encounters simply add variety. The inclusion of people like Scavenger Lords and places like Denandsor and all the abandoned First Age tombs filled with ancient artifacts, deadly traps and bound guardian demons show that these kinds of encounters actually <i>are</i> in theme for the setting. But the idea that I want Exalted played <i>exactly like Pathfinder </i>is absurd <i>because</i> I enjoy Pathfinder so much more; if I want to play a Pathfinder-like game, I'll just <i>go play Pathfinder </i>because it's system is much less frustrating.<br /> <br /> Your accusation that I want these kinds of encounters to be the <i>through line</i> for Exalted campaigns like they are in Pathfinder campaigns is presumptuous and pretentious because I haven't so much as <i>implied that.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, I didn\u2019t list Shadowrun as a game I\u2019ve played before. World of Darkness is a grimdark setting on purpose. There are grim, hopeless elements in Exalted, but it\u2019s hardly <i>the</i> theme of the game like it is in WoD.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-24-2014, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:34:45-07:00","id":291492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291433#post291433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geez man, this shit is bananas. You\u2019ve used a lot of really specific and arrogantly dismissive theorycraft here but, it\u2019s ultimately all for nothing because the Silver Pact\u2019s reaction to the PCs killing Raksi is <i>exactly as severe as the ST wants it to be.</i><br /> <br /> Like:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The more of your posts I read, the more it looks like you don\u2019t <i>play</i> Exalted as much as read the fluff text for its own sake. This level of vagueness is <i>perfect</i> for STs and players for facilitating any kind of game they want, but if one were to treat the setting books as pleasurable reading for their own sake, then yes, I\u2019d imagine writing like this would be very frustrating.<br /> <br /> I think Exalted can stand to have a few (a few!) encounters that are traditional dungeon crawls. The setting is not <i>made worse</i> by having more variety from session to session and different kinds of encounters simply add variety. The inclusion of people like Scavenger Lords and places like Denandsor and all the abandoned First Age tombs filled with ancient artifacts, deadly traps and bound guardian demons show that these kinds of encounters actually <i>are</i> in theme for the setting. But the idea that I want Exalted played <i>exactly like Pathfinder </i>is absurd <i>because</i> I enjoy Pathfinder so much more; if I want to play a Pathfinder-like game, I'll just <i>go play Pathfinder </i>because it's system is much less frustrating.<br /> <br /> Your accusation that I want these kinds of encounters to be the <i>through line</i> for Exalted campaigns like they are in Pathfinder campaigns is presumptuous and pretentious because I haven't so much as <i>implied that.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Also, I didn\u2019t list Shadowrun as a game I\u2019ve played before. World of Darkness is a grimdark setting on purpose. There are grim, hopeless elements in Exalted, but it\u2019s hardly <i>the</i> theme of the game like it is in WoD.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>We want to play Exalted. The key is that we don't want to play the same Exalted that you have in mind. It's not a matter of being grimdark, either, but of being interesting through the complications. Few of us will be entertained by &quot;go there and kill&quot;. Think more Three Kingdoms. Perhaps the Sengoku Jidai can also offer a cogent paradigm - when we play, we don't want the version of Oda Nobunaga that's been smeared for several centuries. We want a character with whom it is interesting to have conflicts. Drinking sake out of skulls or eating babies for the sole purpose of the same is not going to contribute to this desire or scratch this itch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:39:44-07:00","id":291494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291433#post291433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more of your posts I read, the more it looks like you don\u2019t <i>play</i> Exalted as much as read the fluff text for its own sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I know to be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:00:18-07:00","id":291520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291494#post291494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I know to be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a counter argument; all this means is he/she has <i>no excuse</i> for his/her dismissiveness, pretentiousness, and presumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291492#post291492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We want to play Exalted. The key is that we don't want to play the same Exalted that you have in mind. It's not a matter of being grimdark, either, but of being interesting through the complications. Few of us will be entertained by &quot;go there and kill&quot;. Think more Three Kingdoms. Perhaps the Sengoku Jidai can also offer a cogent paradigm - when we play, we don't want the version of Oda Nobunaga that's been smeared for several centuries. We want a character with whom it is interesting to have conflicts. Drinking sake out of skulls or eating babies for the sole purpose of the same is not going to contribute to this desire or scratch this itch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, traditional dungeon crawling isn't the main theme of Exalted, but this setting has Scavenger Lords and empty cities like Denandsor and First Age ruins filled with deadly traps, guardian demons and artifacts for reborn Solars to loot And conveniently Celestial Exalted often have First Age memories that tell them where this stuff is. It's part of Exalted whether you like it or not. And if you don't like it, don't utilize it in your campaigns. But for Pete's sake, don't act like <i>I don't know what Exalted is about </i> if I choose use this stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-24-2014, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T13:52:52-07:00","id":291549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291520#post291520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't a counter argument; all this means is he/she has <i>no excuse</i> for his/her dismissiveness, pretentiousness, and presumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what else is presumptive? Assuming someone doesn't play Exalted, in this Exalted forum. Much bad faith. So insulting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I said, traditional dungeon crawling isn't the main theme of Exalted, but this setting has Scavenger Lords and empty cities like Denandsor and First Age ruins filled with deadly traps, guardian demons and artifacts for reborn Solars to loot And conveniently Celestial Exalted often have First Age memories that tell them where this stuff is. It's part of Exalted whether you like it or not. And if you don't like it, don't utilize it in your campaigns. But for Pete's sake, don't act like <i>I don't know what Exalted is about </i> if I choose use this stuff. </div> </div> </div>Scavenging is not what the issue is over. The issue is over the writing for NPCs. And the writing needs to be interesting, which for the reasons previously stated, it falls short on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:03:08-07:00","id":291556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291520#post291520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, traditional dungeon crawling isn't the main theme of Exalted, but this setting has Scavenger Lords and empty cities like Denandsor and First Age ruins filled with deadly traps, guardian demons and artifacts for reborn Solars to loot</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Raksi living in them?<br /> <br /> Or rather, does the fact that she does mean that her depiction should default to something that presents no difficulties to the matter of fighting her?<br /> <br /> Although personally, I lend little credibility to the idea that the ruins of the prior age and a form of terminology for the people who draw things from them is akin to the lack of context generally inherent to dungeon crawling. It's more like Metroid Prime; there's a story to those ruins that contributes to a larger tone.<br /> <br /> Hell, when Raksi is living there, she's part of that, and it should be just another layer to the idea of her being more than a villain nobody has to feel bad about tearing down.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:10:07-07:00","id":291563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291549#post291549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what else is presumptive? Assuming someone doesn't play Exalted, in this Exalted forum. Much bad faith. So insulting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I presumed nothing; I said \u201c<i>looks like.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291549#post291549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scavenging is not what the issue is over. The issue is over the writing for NPCs. And the writing needs to be interesting, which for the reasons previously stated, it falls short on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn\u2019t make what I said any less valid. If you don\u2019t find an NPC in a setting entertaining you are under no obligation to utilize that NPC than you are to utilize Denandsor, First Age Manses, or Artifact Caches. Even if only 1/5 people find an NPC useful why are you so eager to rain on their parade when you have a plethora of other options? There are plenty of complex, Lunar Elders for you to use instead.<br /> <br /> Raksi\u2019s 2e writeup is conducive to a dungeon crawl and not much else. Because some people like <i>really like </i>dungeon crawls and as I established earlier they <i>are</i> <i>a thing in Exalted</i>, that makes her 2e writeup useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:26:09-07:00","id":291572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291520#post291520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't find an NPC in a setting entertaining you are under no obligation to utilize that NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first, I think that powerful NPCs in a setting like Creation, in a system with the themes of Exalted, should be written to maximize use across as many hypothetical games as possible. Not just assume that every ST will use Ma-Ha-Suchi (for example) as a insane-body-horror boss fight. Some STs will use him for a boss fight and in such a circumstance a detailed stat block is useful. Some groups will want to enter into alliances or bargains or try to trick and subvert his goals, and for them a combat-oriented statblock or a one-dimensional write-up of &quot;this guy is an Obvious Villain, note the obvious villainy he has done&quot; is a lot less useful than a clear statement of what fires this guy has his irons in. <i>The game should orient to provide maximum value to both of those extremes and anything in between.</i><br /> <br /> For a game like Exalted, where Big Bads <i>typically</i> are assumed to have more depth and deeper goals than &quot;evil wizard hiding in a dungeon sending zombies and skeletons up to kill people to have more bodies with which to make skeletons and zombies, because evil wizards are dicks, something something Orcus&quot; then I think it's really valuable for the written game books to be written broadly enough that there can be all kinds of plots written for Raksi other than &quot;wow she sucks and is a baby-eating psycho, murder Raksi kthx.&quot; It doesn't matter if you ultimately use her for a boss fight. You're basically suggesting &quot;I did this and this was fun ergo this is what the default should be.&quot; And then you're calling other people arrogant and presumptive?<br /> <br /> It's easy enough for an ST to look at a hypothetical long and nuanced depiction of Raksi, her past, and her goals (or Ma-Ha, or Chejop, or for that matter Dace or Iron Siaka or <i>whoever</i>) and say &quot;nahhhh I don't need any of this, I need a boss fight to cap off this arc, and Raksi fits well enough to be behind the Bad Shit the PCs have been preventing.&quot; <i>Please note that nobody is saying that using an NPC like that is BadWrongFun.</i><br /> <br /> However it's less easy for an ST to look at a statblock and a weak paragraph of one-dimensional motivations that are all focused on &quot;this person is Eeeeeevil with a capital E, see look at her eating babies, look at her daddy issues, that's all there is that we care to say about it&quot; and determine how else they can use this person <i>except as</i> a boss fight?<br /> <br /> Hell, in settings where there <i>is </i>evil more objective than baby-eating (see: Glorantha, with entities/groups like Ralzakark, Delecti, Sheng Seleris, the God Learners...) the setting presumes that other entities in-setting have reasons to truck with them (if only to keep them busy or redirect them, or be the dog on your leash instead of the wolf at your door). The inherent assumption is that PCs can be involved in those devils' deals and further them or work to kill these monsters, <i>and the monsters' write-ups plausibly support either, depending on what faction your group is affiliated with</i>. But the default is there (the Lunar Empire says &quot;sure that guy is the greatest and most powerful and objectively-evil monsters ever to exist, who sucked at the teat of one of the greatest evil gods to ever walk the earth, and we <i>could</i> divert our resources to kill him, <i>buuuut </i>he keeps the other 40,000 broos in Dorastor in line <i>and </i>he actually abides by his contracts...sure, we can kill him at our leisure if we choose to send an army into that hellhole, but right now he's not near as high on the priority list as stamping out rebellions on the route to our newly-conquered giant port&quot;).<br /> <br /> You have moral choice, action, and consequence all in there together. Kill Ralzakark and suddenly you have 40,000 chaos monsters with no terribly-feared leader to keep them in line and you've well and proper fucked every region that borders Dorastor. Leave him be and he's literally a cancer on the world <i>but</i> you effectively have all those broos in check just hanging out, posing less of an immediate danger to you than the numerous, successful barbarian insurgencies along the trade routes. Hell, negotiate better terms to that agreement and he might even help you with your barbarian problem since he fucking <i>hates</i> their gods.<br /> <br /> That's the kind of shit Exalted <i>should have</i>, especially with its Big Name NPCs. Having many options to pick from is better than &quot;let's just write Raksi as a stereotypical evil thing to Boss Fight,&quot; even if that's what you wind up using her for and have fun doing it. How do you even argue that providing more options to make an NPC more useful to more groups is not an inherently better state? Having Raksi be evil in a vacuum is just pretty dumb and doesn't provide help for any STs except those who decide to use her as a boss fight. A write up only conducive to use as a dungeon crawl is pretty much worthless <i>unless you intend to do a dungeon crawl</i>, and that sucks for anyone hoping for tips on how to run Raksi as anything other than someone you can unrepentantly murder without feeling bad about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-24-2014, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:39:21-07:00","id":291581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291563#post291563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presumed nothing; I said \u201c<i>looks like.\u201d</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, am going to presume that you're too old for this form of sophistry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi\u2019s 2e writeup is conducive to a dungeon crawl and not much else. Because some people like <i>really like </i>dungeon crawls and as I established earlier they <i>are</i> <i>a thing in Exalted</i>, that makes her 2e writeup useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're presenting a false dichotomy in the idea that presenting a character as having broader applicability as robbing one of the capacity to give them straightforward narrative roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:41:55-07:00","id":291583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291556#post291556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Raksi living in them?</div> </div> </div> </div>She\u2019s probably living in Mahalanka because she wants privacy to study the <i>Book of Three Circles</i> and because she finds living as a god-queen among ape-men <i>fun.</i> It\u2019s the City of a Thousand Golden Delights for Raksi only; of course she\u2019s living there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291556#post291556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather, does the fact that she does mean that her depiction should default to something that presents no difficulties to the matter of fighting her?<br /> <br /> Although personally, I lend little credibility to the idea that the ruins of the prior age and a form of terminology for the people who draw things from them is akin to the lack of context generally inherent to dungeon crawling. It's more like Metroid Prime; there's a story to those ruins that contributes to a larger tone.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of context is not inherent to dungeon crawling. Just because you have a reason in Metroid Prime to enter a dungeon doesn\u2019t disqualify it from being a dungeon crawl.<br /> <br /> You enter the Ruins of Harrowstone because the restless dead there will murder everyone in the nearby town of Ravengro if you don\u2019t <i>do something</i> about it.<br /> <br /> You enter the Citadel of Dresen to reclaim it for the Mendevian Crusade and cleanse Fallen Sarkoris of its demonic occupiers.<br /> <br /> You enter Thistletop to stop Nualia from sacrificing a bunch of innocent people to her profane goddess to complete her abyssal apotheosis. <br /> <br /> These things are still dungeon crawls; games with dungeon crawling usually have context for those dungeon crawls. The &quot;difficulties to the matter of fighting her&quot; are <i>you might die</i> because she has an army of Ape-folk and can summon Second Circle Demons. Unless the fight ends up being trivially easy...<br /> <br /> ...then that's just bad encounter design.<br /> <br /> Additionally, as I said earlier, her connection to the Silver Pact and vise-versa is left <i>really vague </i>and that's probably on purpose; it means the Silver Pact's reaction to you killing Raksi is <i>exactly as severe as the ST wants it to be.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:53:28-07:00","id":291587,"title":"","content":"Ranger_Lord, I don't mean this as any sort of attack, but you really should back away from this thread or tone the language way down. I agree with some of your points, but you're making them in a very antagonistic way that's failing to get anyone on your side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291492#post291492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We want to play Exalted. The key is that we don't want to play the same Exalted that you have in mind. It's not a matter of being grimdark, either, but of being interesting through the complications. Few of us will be entertained by &quot;go there and kill&quot;. Think more Three Kingdoms. Perhaps the Sengoku Jidai can also offer a cogent paradigm - when we play, we don't want the version of Oda Nobunaga that's been smeared for several centuries. We want a character with whom it is interesting to have conflicts. Drinking sake out of skulls or eating babies for the sole purpose of the same is not going to contribute to this desire or scratch this itch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to comment on this. I've had GM's where the PC's could never get a clean victory because there were always unforseen consequences, bigger fish, somebody's master plan that we were just playing into, etc. And while some of that was fine, in the end, too much of it just felt frustrating and dis-empowering because it never felt like we were accomplishing anything or getting closer to any sort of goal, though we were allegedly powerful. Balance is everything--alongside moral relativism and unforseen consequences, characters should have some straightforward goals, and the odd clean, satisfying victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:00:15-07:00","id":291604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291581#post291581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I, on the other hand, am going to presume that you're too old for this form of sophistry.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't sophistry; I <i>honestly </i><i>hoped</i>, if Blaque was just reading these books for pleasure instead of using them for their intended purpose he'd see that section and think &quot;Oh, geez, I'm totally in the wrong here,&quot; and drop it. Just because that didn't end up happening doesn't mean I was any <i>less sincere </i>about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291581#post291581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're presenting a false dichotomy in the idea that presenting a character as having broader applicability as robbing one of the capacity to give them straightforward narrative roles.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I am doing no such thing; I'm arguing against the <i>sado</i><i>masochistic notion</i> that the <i>inarguable canon </i><i>implications</i> of killing Raksi should <i>always outweigh</i> or <i>always nearly outweigh </i>the potential problems you solve by killing her. If they are then going through all that trouble doesn't feel satisfying<i>.</i> Since my use of these terms are being taken so seriously, I will concede that I <i>should have</i> put quotes around the words &quot;complex&quot; and &quot;nuanced&quot; when I talked about this because sarcasm does not come across well in textual form otherwise. I didn't think I needed to though because <i>who the hell</i> actually thinks making a character an uncomfortable, narrative roadblock makes them more complex or nuanced?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-24-2014, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:46:54-07:00","id":291621,"title":"","content":"Dipping in right quick as I'm in the middle of grading some papers currently, I just wanted to point out that allegations that I only read the books for pleasure is patently false. I have been playing and running Exalted since 2001 in a fairly constant capacity until about June last year when waiting for 3e kicked in and I moved. I intend to pick up and run a game right when 3e is out and already have a pretty big OneNote document with a few webs of influence, power players and encounters setup sight unseen of what I want to run.<br /> <br /> So no, I don't just read Exalted for pleasure. And no, I don't just want more complication for an enjoyable sit-and-read. I'll address your points further in a bit when I get a couple papers done. Until then others have already done a lot in what I have been saying fairly nicely. <br /> <br /> And while waiting, even granting that I were simply reading for pleasure, I will point you at the concept of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tu_quoque\" target=\"_blank\"><i>tu quoque</i></a> to think about a bit when discussing whether accusing me of running or playing the game disqualifies me from discussing how it might be made more playable.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:51:25-07:00","id":291624,"title":"","content":"This is the second time I see the argument &quot;you don't actually play the games, you just read the books&quot; used as shorthand to dismiss someone's opinion as irrelevant to the &quot;REAL&quot; Exalted players. It pisses me off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T17:09:20-07:00","id":291646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291624#post291624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the second time I see the argument &quot;you don't actually play the games, you just read the books&quot; used as shorthand to dismiss someone's opinion as irrelevant to the &quot;REAL&quot; Exalted players. It pisses me off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never dismissed anyone\u2019s opinion as irrelevant because of their experience level. This is the bit of conversation being referenced:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291433#post291433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more of your posts I read, the more it looks like you don\u2019t <i>play</i> Exalted as much as read the fluff text for its own sake. This level of vagueness is <i>perfect</i> for STs and players for facilitating any kind of game they want, but if one were to treat the setting books as pleasurable reading for their own sake, then yes, I\u2019d imagine writing like this would be very frustrating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used allegory (hence &quot;it looks like&quot;) to try to get people to look at Raksi\u2019s writeup for its intended purpose, which I didn\u2019t feel like they were doing. I didn\u2019t offhandedly dismiss anything; some people just don't seem to be able to argue with me in this thread without putting words in my mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 10-24-2014, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T23:18:54-07:00","id":291828,"title":"","content":"What I want to know is, was that image drawn AROUND the cutouts of the faces, or is there a barbie doll level of detail under them, or are they <i>actually</i> censoring something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:21:13-07:00","id":292246,"title":"","content":"Inquiring minds want to know!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>1","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27-ulfsarkar","name":"Ulfsarkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T11:34:41-07:00","id":292258,"title":"","content":"I want to say something funny but can't really think of anything so I suppose it's time for the truth: They all have Ken anatomy down there :cries:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T21:10:54-07:00","id":292650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=291334#post291334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to think of examples of cases where people interact with a large and fearsome figure who has probably eaten some of their own kind without it being a moral judgement issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you look for that?<br /> <br /> It is absolutely supposed to be a moral judgment issue in Exalted. I mean, you can choose to ignore it for any one of a number of reasons, or you could agree with Raksi and decide that since she's Exalted she has the right to eat mortals, but the game isn't supposed to help you avoid the moral problems inherent in eating people, and I seriously doubt, when looking for inspirations or whatever, any of the writers have ever said &quot;now, what source can I draw on to minimize the moral issues in this story?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:36:40-07:00","id":292723,"title":"","content":"There are I think three explicit dungeon crawls in Exalted? They're all pretty bad. The style of the game is just not well suited to something like that -- the game works too hard to encourage off-the-rails solutions to problems, and to motivate players to weigh options other than the &quot;default&quot;. It's fine to set something up as good fodder for a dungeon crawl, but you can't get overly detailed about it, or assume the players will do the &quot;right&quot; thing in the &quot;right&quot; way, or you're likely to be caught by surprise. A lot of this is a thematic issue: one of the basic things going on with Exalted is that you play a highly empowered character, and the game tries to make you feel empowered by allowing your actions to have dramatic effects on your surroundings, and by having you make decisions and ensuring that the decisions are meaningful. Dungeon crawls have a lot of friction with these themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:50:17-07:00","id":292731,"title":"","content":"Fillial Wisdom, the Essence 6 Elder Dawn Caste whose life is spent sitting in the middle of a ruined temple at the heart of the jungle being vaguely, non-specifically evil, with a unique super-form mode, and armies composed of Goblins and Hobgoblins (these are their literal names, I shit you not), and whose city is also overrun by (evil) leech gods and (feral) dragon-kings, is the archetypal Exalted dungeon raid boss.<br /> <br /> I mean for the love of god, Ruins of Rathess includes stats for an ooze monster.<br /> <br /> AN OOZE.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T01:35:51-07:00","id":292793,"title":"","content":"And The Labyrinth could totally be described as The World's Greatest Dungeon, of Doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T01:39:08-07:00","id":292794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=292650#post292650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you look for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frame of reference for how a sympathetic character might interact with such figures with an awareness of their transgression, but without making it a central issue of the interaction.<br /> <br /> Another example that just occurred to me; journalists interacting with members of organised crime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is absolutely supposed to be a moral judgment issue in Exalted. I mean, you can choose to ignore it for any one of a number of reasons</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the point where one says &quot;I'm privately morally judging you, but I'm keeping that to myself and not letting it express itself through my words and actions&quot; is where I might call a little bit of bullshit on the relevance of their convictions, excepting cases where active deception is involved for the sake of some later opportune moment. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:55:03-07:00","id":292972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=292793#post292793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And The Labyrinth could totally be described as The World's Greatest Dungeon, of Doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can try and chip away at the Infinite Prison, but I don't think you're going to inflict enough damage to disrupt it before it gets bored and leaves. Also, House of Succulent Tears. The Labyrinth is in need of some refurbishment. Preferably which doesn't involve rape victim ghosts raping rapists, along with whomever else the Lover wants to hand over to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T08:36:06-07:00","id":292980,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but you have corridors after corridors of traps and horrors. At least at some places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T15:55:18-07:00","id":297572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/285023-~-first-age-lunar-elder-best-written-characters-ever-~-nsft-maybe?p=292972#post292972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can try and chip away at the Infinite Prison, but I don't think you're going to inflict enough damage to disrupt it before it gets bored and leaves. Also, House of Succulent Tears. The Labyrinth is in need of some refurbishment. Preferably which doesn't involve rape victim ghosts raping rapists, along with whomever else the Lover wants to hand over to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Labyrinth should in places carry theme's of Dante's Inferno and judeo-christian ideas of hell and purgatory, this carries well with the very gothic theme of the Underworld. I maintain that some of the dead Solars rather than succumbing to Lethe, or embracing the Neverborn, carve a pocket of their own in the Labyrinth which they punish those of their brand of wicked. Don't forget Zhokai the City of Genocides was pretty awesome too. There needs to be more realms of oblivion worshippers, and the tomb bodies of the Neverborn too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}